1
00:06:31,025 --> 00:06:33,145
I demand an explanation, sir.

2
00:06:33,625 --> 00:06:34,985
Answer me.

3
00:06:39,545 --> 00:06:42,065
Answers are a response
to questions, Vicky.

4
00:06:43,465 --> 00:06:46,785
Demands are either accepted
or rejected.

5
00:06:48,665 --> 00:06:50,065
Which I have already done.

6
00:06:50,305 --> 00:06:52,065
Why didn't you do it yourself?

7
00:06:52,385 --> 00:06:55,705
Why did you reject my thesis
in an email to the vice chancellor?

8
00:06:57,545 --> 00:06:59,305
It's a question this time, sir.

9
00:06:59,745 --> 00:07:01,025
You must answer.

10
00:07:02,305 --> 00:07:03,585
Personal development.

11
00:07:04,825 --> 00:07:06,345
Character building.

12
00:07:07,545 --> 00:07:09,185
Building the nation.

13
00:07:10,905 --> 00:07:12,305
Remember what it means?

14
00:07:12,425 --> 00:07:13,425
Of course.

15
00:07:13,945 --> 00:07:15,945
If you hadn't rejected it...

16
00:07:16,065 --> 00:07:20,025
Then the primary subject of my thesis
would have been these RSS slogans.

17
00:07:20,345 --> 00:07:21,385
Slogans?

18
00:07:21,865 --> 00:07:23,545
This is your problem, Vicky.

19
00:07:25,385 --> 00:07:27,145
I asked you the meaning.

20
00:07:28,385 --> 00:07:29,905
And you're giving me references.

21
00:07:30,745 --> 00:07:32,065
That too wrong ones.

22
00:07:33,665 --> 00:07:35,305
These are not slogans.

23
00:07:37,025 --> 00:07:39,705
These are the three veins
of the Sangh.

24
00:07:41,865 --> 00:07:44,985
Each swayamsevak's patriotism...

25
00:07:46,745 --> 00:07:49,185
runs through them.

26
00:07:50,025 --> 00:07:52,705
I had taught you all this
three years ago.

27
00:07:53,345 --> 00:07:55,505
I had taught you something else too.

28
00:07:57,625 --> 00:07:58,865
Do you remember or...

29
00:07:59,025 --> 00:08:00,025
I remember.

30
00:08:01,065 --> 00:08:03,465
But until these three things
are done

31
00:08:03,745 --> 00:08:05,025
the work will be incomplete.

32
00:08:05,145 --> 00:08:08,505
It has nothing to do with
the rejection of my thesis.

33
00:08:08,825 --> 00:08:09,825
It does.

34
00:08:11,465 --> 00:08:17,345
I'm tired of trying to develop you
as a person.

35
00:08:18,945 --> 00:08:20,465
But you...

36
00:08:21,945 --> 00:08:24,025
You couldn't build your character.

37
00:08:26,905 --> 00:08:28,865
These are not my signatures.

38
00:08:33,625 --> 00:08:38,505
And yet you mentioned me
as your guide in your thesis.

39
00:08:39,945 --> 00:08:41,185
I know why.

40
00:08:42,425 --> 00:08:45,545
Because the path
this guide showed you

41
00:08:47,305 --> 00:08:49,185
you were going
in the opposite direction.

42
00:08:50,545 --> 00:08:51,545
That's why...

43
00:08:52,185 --> 00:08:55,345
That's why
I got your thesis rejected.

44
00:08:56,505 --> 00:08:58,385
And I'll do it ten more times.

45
00:08:58,505 --> 00:08:59,865
Do whatever you want.

46
00:09:02,745 --> 00:09:06,305
"Ekam sat, vipr bahuda vadanti".

47
00:09:08,065 --> 00:09:09,585
There is only one Truth, sir.

48
00:09:10,145 --> 00:09:12,945
But wise men believe
that there are many truths.

49
00:09:14,065 --> 00:09:16,945
This is something
you've taught me.

50
00:09:17,385 --> 00:09:19,785
There might be multiple paths
leading to the truth.

51
00:09:20,305 --> 00:09:21,985
But if the destination is Truth

52
00:09:23,145 --> 00:09:27,545
then it's our responsibility to
remove all the obstacles on the way.

53
00:09:30,625 --> 00:09:32,904
Our paths are very different, sir.

54
00:09:32,905 --> 00:09:36,625
There was only one obstacle
on my path.

55
00:09:36,945 --> 00:09:38,225
This signature.

56
00:09:39,825 --> 00:09:41,545
I have removed that too.

57
00:09:42,545 --> 00:09:43,865
Did I do something wrong?

58
00:09:44,305 --> 00:09:45,305
Tell me, sir.

59
00:09:45,545 --> 00:09:47,065
What was my mistake?

60
00:09:47,825 --> 00:09:51,465
And if I have done something wrong,
prove it.

61
00:09:51,825 --> 00:09:54,825
If you can prove it,
I'll back off.

62
00:09:56,865 --> 00:09:59,345
If you can't prove it...

63
00:10:00,545 --> 00:10:04,745
then you're no one to stop me
in this independent nation.

64
00:10:04,905 --> 00:10:05,705
Who are you?

65
00:10:13,345 --> 00:10:15,265
I'm not stopping you, Vicky.

66
00:10:16,625 --> 00:10:18,825
I'm rectifying my mistake.

67
00:10:20,345 --> 00:10:22,065
Because you are my mistake.

68
00:10:30,065 --> 00:10:30,825
Sir!

69
00:10:32,545 --> 00:10:34,225
- Stop filming.
- Sir!

70
00:10:34,585 --> 00:10:35,465
Sir.

71
00:10:39,665 --> 00:10:44,465
This is not your classroom where
you can just say class dismissed.

72
00:10:45,345 --> 00:10:47,185
The conversation has just started.

73
00:10:47,625 --> 00:10:48,625
Vicky.

74
00:10:49,025 --> 00:10:50,345
Stop this circus.

75
00:10:50,545 --> 00:10:51,465
Leave right now.

76
00:10:51,665 --> 00:10:52,985
I want to leave, sir.

77
00:10:53,385 --> 00:10:55,785
But he has rejected my thesis.

78
00:10:56,825 --> 00:10:58,705
Along with my thesis...

79
00:11:00,065 --> 00:11:02,065
he wants to block
my new way of thinking.

80
00:11:07,225 --> 00:11:09,345
It's your bad luck, sir.

81
00:11:10,265 --> 00:11:13,625
You can use your power
to stop the publication of my thesis

82
00:11:13,945 --> 00:11:15,265
but not my voice.

83
00:11:15,665 --> 00:11:17,505
Is this a film shoot?

84
00:11:18,465 --> 00:11:20,385
- Stop the camera.
- Why, sir?

85
00:11:22,305 --> 00:11:23,145
Why should we stop?

86
00:11:24,625 --> 00:11:28,465
You're doing all this to protect
your beloved RSS.

87
00:11:46,065 --> 00:11:47,584
- Did you record that?
- Yes, ma'am.

88
00:11:47,585 --> 00:11:48,625
Show me.

89
00:11:50,465 --> 00:11:52,225
- Share it with me, okay.
- Okay.

90
00:12:03,745 --> 00:12:05,185
May I come in, sir?

91
00:12:07,185 --> 00:12:08,865
Sir, I'm Vicky Hegde.

92
00:12:09,345 --> 00:12:10,425
Your student.

93
00:12:12,145 --> 00:12:16,225
Sir, I want to write a thesis
on the history of the RSS.

94
00:12:16,665 --> 00:12:18,185
On the hundred years of the RSS.

95
00:12:18,585 --> 00:12:22,505
And no one better to guide me
on this topic but you.

96
00:12:23,545 --> 00:12:25,185
Will you please help me?

97
00:12:25,505 --> 00:12:27,145
Do you even know

98
00:12:28,465 --> 00:12:30,385
who established the Sangh?

99
00:12:30,785 --> 00:12:33,745
Dr. Keshavrao Baliram Hedgewar.

100
00:12:34,185 --> 00:12:36,785
Born 1889, April.

101
00:13:43,305 --> 00:13:47,705
Are you writing a thesis
or making a hodgepodge?

102
00:13:48,265 --> 00:13:51,065
It's not a hodgepodge.
It's a 12-course meal.

103
00:13:52,225 --> 00:13:53,465
And I can assure you, sir

104
00:13:53,665 --> 00:13:57,785
my thesis will reveal
a lot of hidden truths

105
00:13:58,065 --> 00:13:59,665
about the history of the RSS.

106
00:15:10,345 --> 00:15:14,025
(students protesting)

107
00:15:29,185 --> 00:15:32,145
Sir, you're fighting against
your professor and the Sangh.

108
00:15:32,745 --> 00:15:35,305
An educational institute
is dedicated to Goddess Saraswati...

109
00:15:35,665 --> 00:15:36,785
Please tell us why.

110
00:15:37,625 --> 00:15:39,785
Both of us worship Saraswati,
the goddess of knowledge.

111
00:15:39,945 --> 00:15:41,665
But no matter
how beautiful the idol is

112
00:15:41,865 --> 00:15:44,745
if it's covered in dust
then it can't be worshipped.

113
00:15:44,945 --> 00:15:46,865
What does that have to do
with the Sangh?

114
00:15:47,185 --> 00:15:49,624
Many swayamsevaks

115
00:15:49,625 --> 00:15:54,505
are propagating their ideologies
in schools, colleges...

116
00:15:54,705 --> 00:15:56,585
They're trying to fool us too.

117
00:15:56,705 --> 00:15:58,585
They've been lying to us for years.

118
00:15:59,665 --> 00:16:03,184
Every time new India has
raised their voice...

119
00:16:03,185 --> 00:16:04,985
they've been systematically silenced.

120
00:16:05,185 --> 00:16:07,425
What exactly is your thesis about?

121
00:16:08,785 --> 00:16:10,545
The truth about the RSS is my thesis.

122
00:16:10,785 --> 00:16:12,145
The truth they've hidden for years.

123
00:16:12,585 --> 00:16:14,225
But I'm going to unmask the truth.

124
00:16:14,385 --> 00:16:17,785
Your thesis has been rejected.
What do you have to say about that?

125
00:16:18,905 --> 00:16:21,065
No one can reject my thesis now.

126
00:16:21,385 --> 00:16:22,785
And no one can silence me.

127
00:16:23,065 --> 00:16:25,585
What about your own teacher
slapping you?

128
00:16:26,025 --> 00:16:27,825
He didn't just slap me.

129
00:16:28,145 --> 00:16:32,865
He slapped every Indian citizen
who dared to seek the truth. Got it?

130
00:16:34,545 --> 00:16:35,825
But my thesis...

131
00:16:35,985 --> 00:16:37,625
...will expose the RSS.

132
00:16:38,225 --> 00:16:41,065
The RSS is
an anti-national organisation.

133
00:16:41,305 --> 00:16:42,905
How can you call the RSS--

134
00:16:45,305 --> 00:16:47,545
Do they even know what
anti-national means?

135
00:16:49,585 --> 00:16:53,185
A group that has not picked up
weapons in the last 100 years.

136
00:16:53,505 --> 00:16:54,585
They are...

137
00:16:55,865 --> 00:16:56,865
Anyway...

138
00:17:02,305 --> 00:17:03,224
And you?

139
00:17:03,225 --> 00:17:04,705
Why are you surprised?

140
00:17:07,265 --> 00:17:12,825
Prabha, in life either you win
or you learn a lesson.

141
00:17:14,065 --> 00:17:16,785
And there's only one lesson
in our life.

142
00:17:19,945 --> 00:17:24,505
Don't get too used
to the good times.

143
00:17:28,465 --> 00:17:30,305
It'll eventually leave you in tears.

144
00:17:35,785 --> 00:17:36,785
Let me see.

145
00:17:38,025 --> 00:17:39,545
I'll put some ointment at night.

146
00:17:39,665 --> 00:17:40,905
It'll be fine by morning.

147
00:17:43,265 --> 00:17:43,945
Prabha.

148
00:17:53,385 --> 00:17:55,425
So many years of pain.

149
00:17:56,145 --> 00:17:58,345
Can it be healed overnight?

150
00:18:00,345 --> 00:18:03,705
When we carry some pain
for years...

151
00:18:05,145 --> 00:18:08,545
Unknowingly, we make it our own.

152
00:18:09,505 --> 00:18:11,745
We help them grow with care.

153
00:18:12,745 --> 00:18:14,305
Then it doesn't hurt so much.

154
00:18:45,745 --> 00:18:48,225
On time.
Very good.

155
00:18:49,265 --> 00:18:50,345
Shut the door.

156
00:19:04,345 --> 00:19:06,745
The path you've chosen, Vicky...

157
00:19:07,945 --> 00:19:12,145
You need to keep an open mind for that.
But behind closed doors.

158
00:19:13,425 --> 00:19:14,785
Start training now.

159
00:19:15,145 --> 00:19:16,945
You'll find it handy later on.
Okay?

160
00:19:17,985 --> 00:19:18,985
Thank you, Vicky.

161
00:19:20,625 --> 00:19:24,145
One needs guts to do
what you did. Right?

162
00:19:26,025 --> 00:19:30,265
That one slap made you
shake up the entire system.

163
00:19:33,385 --> 00:19:35,465
Ma'am, one doesn't need guts
to get slapped.

164
00:19:36,745 --> 00:19:37,624
Only jaws.

165
00:19:37,625 --> 00:19:39,625
- Ipshita!
- Yes.

166
00:19:39,745 --> 00:19:43,625
Where's the thesis index
I'd asked for?

167
00:19:46,265 --> 00:19:49,265
Whether my instructions are
written or spoken...

168
00:19:49,985 --> 00:19:51,465
Don't you ever cut them.

169
00:19:52,505 --> 00:19:53,505
Yes, ma'am.

170
00:19:56,305 --> 00:20:01,065
So, Vicky, you should keep
an open mind now. Right?

171
00:20:02,065 --> 00:20:05,825
Because until now
you were under Nadkarni's wing.

172
00:20:06,425 --> 00:20:10,585
He narrates the written truth
quite well. I mean...

173
00:20:10,985 --> 00:20:12,025
With all due respect.

174
00:20:15,785 --> 00:20:17,665
But once you're under my wing

175
00:20:17,865 --> 00:20:22,145
you'll learn that truth
doesn't need to be narrated.

176
00:20:23,065 --> 00:20:26,145
Narratives need to be turned
into truth.

177
00:20:26,825 --> 00:20:27,705
Noted, ma'am.

178
00:20:29,665 --> 00:20:32,825
By the way, which one is your wing?

179
00:20:33,425 --> 00:20:35,024
Right wing or--

180
00:20:35,025 --> 00:20:37,585
Left is always right.

181
00:20:45,865 --> 00:20:48,585
And ma'am, thank you.

182
00:20:48,865 --> 00:20:52,225
For making my "slap video" go viral.

183
00:20:54,425 --> 00:20:55,425
Good night.

184
00:20:57,585 --> 00:21:00,945
Ma'am, he thinks you made
the video go viral. Meaning?

185
00:21:02,665 --> 00:21:05,145
Meaning he doesn't
only have an open mind.

186
00:21:06,505 --> 00:21:07,505
But a sharp mind too.

187
00:21:14,905 --> 00:21:16,705
Hey!
What?

188
00:21:16,825 --> 00:21:18,865
Vicky, please don't get involved
with them.

189
00:21:19,305 --> 00:21:21,665
They're supporting you now
because you're in the news.

190
00:21:22,305 --> 00:21:25,745
When you fall none of them
will come to your rescue.

191
00:21:26,025 --> 00:21:29,065
So, Saara, you're confident
that I'll fall.

192
00:21:30,385 --> 00:21:31,544
I'm not going to fall.

193
00:21:31,545 --> 00:21:34,864
And even if I do
these people will pull me up.

194
00:21:34,865 --> 00:21:35,665
Got it?

195
00:21:36,345 --> 00:21:38,185
Prof. Nadkarni always said...

196
00:21:38,825 --> 00:21:40,185
If we fall

197
00:21:40,345 --> 00:21:44,385
it makes a huge difference
who helps up get back up.

198
00:21:44,505 --> 00:21:47,145
Maybe it made a difference to him.
Makes no difference to me.

199
00:21:47,785 --> 00:21:49,345
Saara, I need to reach my goal.

200
00:21:49,945 --> 00:21:55,184
I don't care if the car that takes me
there is red, saffron or green--

201
00:21:55,185 --> 00:21:56,545
It does make a difference, Vicky!

202
00:21:57,785 --> 00:21:59,065
They're not right.

203
00:21:59,385 --> 00:22:02,505
Whoever takes me to my destination
is right for me.

204
00:22:03,145 --> 00:22:03,905
Got it?

205
00:22:07,865 --> 00:22:11,545
Mumbai Institute of Arts and Economics
student, Vicky's actions today

206
00:22:11,665 --> 00:22:14,345
has sent shockwaves
that will be felt in Delhi too.

207
00:22:14,505 --> 00:22:18,385
Viral video sensation, Vicky Hegde,
one slap and a revolution.

208
00:22:18,505 --> 00:22:20,944
On social media, #JusticeforVicky

209
00:22:20,945 --> 00:22:24,464
and #MumbaiCollegeCrisis are trending.

210
00:22:24,465 --> 00:22:25,464
The video where Vicky...

211
00:22:25,465 --> 00:22:29,304
talks about removing
the dust has millions of views.

212
00:22:29,305 --> 00:22:31,345
Students have launched a digital war.

213
00:22:31,505 --> 00:22:34,625
Universities across the world
have shown support for Vicky.

214
00:22:34,825 --> 00:22:39,145
Is it safe for just one student to go
against such a big organisation?

215
00:22:39,305 --> 00:22:41,345
Vicky said he'll not back off.

216
00:22:41,505 --> 00:22:43,505
(students protesting)

217
00:23:21,505 --> 00:23:24,785
Look, we should restrict this here.

218
00:23:25,305 --> 00:23:28,745
No one will gain anything by washing
dirty linen in public.

219
00:23:29,665 --> 00:23:31,225
Vicky, you want respect.

220
00:23:31,425 --> 00:23:33,545
I'll give it you.
I assure you.

221
00:23:34,745 --> 00:23:37,065
Nadkarni, you have problems
with the camera?

222
00:23:37,785 --> 00:23:39,345
I'll give you the assurance.

223
00:23:39,905 --> 00:23:43,225
No cameras. No CCTV.
Closed rooms.

224
00:23:43,385 --> 00:23:46,545
Nadkarni, Vicky,
do you agree?

225
00:23:47,345 --> 00:23:49,865
We'll decide everything here.

226
00:23:52,225 --> 00:23:52,905
Ready?

227
00:23:57,145 --> 00:23:59,064
Okay.
It's decided then.

228
00:23:59,065 --> 00:24:00,265
Let's finish this now.

229
00:24:03,865 --> 00:24:05,505
Ma'am, we have a problem.

230
00:24:05,825 --> 00:24:07,824
VC is convincing him
for a closed-door meeting.

231
00:24:07,825 --> 00:24:09,025
He'll compromise.

232
00:24:09,185 --> 00:24:12,385
Didn't I tell you to send
more people to the fountain?

233
00:24:13,265 --> 00:24:14,385
Did you?

234
00:24:14,945 --> 00:24:17,425
Ma'am, you're not listening to me.
He'll give in.

235
00:24:20,385 --> 00:24:23,465
Didn't you hear him
clearly yesterday?

236
00:24:25,065 --> 00:24:27,985
If I've understood him even a little

237
00:24:28,945 --> 00:24:31,545
then he'll not let anything happen
behind closed doors.

238
00:24:33,665 --> 00:24:34,945
You know why, Ipshita?

239
00:24:35,625 --> 00:24:36,865
Because he's a bomb.

240
00:24:36,985 --> 00:24:38,825
And bombs only know one thing.

241
00:24:39,905 --> 00:24:40,785
Boom!

242
00:24:45,425 --> 00:24:46,425
Vicky is here.

243
00:24:46,545 --> 00:24:48,145
(indistinct chatter)

244
00:24:51,905 --> 00:24:52,905
Sir.

245
00:24:53,665 --> 00:24:56,545
We'll talk behind closed doors.

246
00:24:57,145 --> 00:25:00,185
But sir, I have five questions.

247
00:25:00,745 --> 00:25:05,065
If you answer those,
I'll take my thesis back.

248
00:25:12,825 --> 00:25:14,385
Where are you going, sir?

249
00:25:15,185 --> 00:25:16,865
The class is about to begin.

250
00:25:18,505 --> 00:25:20,984
Sir, what's the hurry?

251
00:25:20,985 --> 00:25:22,065
Hold on.

252
00:25:23,025 --> 00:25:24,025
Sir.

253
00:25:25,545 --> 00:25:26,945
Sir, please stop.

254
00:25:27,305 --> 00:25:29,145
There's one more class
you must teach.

255
00:25:29,305 --> 00:25:31,945
Sir! Sir!
One minute, sir! One minute!

256
00:25:37,385 --> 00:25:39,465
Looks like you're in a rush.

257
00:25:40,865 --> 00:25:44,865
Sir, you call yourself my guide.
My guru.

258
00:25:45,945 --> 00:25:47,905
I've asked you five questions.

259
00:25:48,505 --> 00:25:50,745
And if you can answer them...

260
00:25:51,985 --> 00:25:53,065
I'll disappear.

261
00:25:53,745 --> 00:25:56,825
But if you fail to answer even
one question...

262
00:25:57,665 --> 00:26:00,705
Then the truth about the RSS
will come out in the open.

263
00:26:01,065 --> 00:26:02,305
My question is...

264
00:26:02,425 --> 00:26:03,825
Do you accept this challenge?

265
00:26:07,705 --> 00:26:08,705
What happened, sir?

266
00:26:09,065 --> 00:26:10,424
Why are you so quiet?

267
00:26:10,425 --> 00:26:11,745
Why aren't you saying anything?

268
00:26:13,865 --> 00:26:15,985
Take this megaphone.

269
00:26:16,985 --> 00:26:18,345
Talk through this.

270
00:26:18,545 --> 00:26:20,825
Anyway, you are a mouthpiece
for the RSS.

271
00:26:25,945 --> 00:26:28,185
Do you see this Nataraj idol, Vicky?

272
00:26:29,505 --> 00:26:31,625
Can you all see this Nataraj idol?

273
00:26:34,865 --> 00:26:36,785
What is under his feet?

274
00:26:37,505 --> 00:26:39,545
Most people often think
it's a child.

275
00:26:40,665 --> 00:26:41,825
It's not a child.

276
00:26:42,265 --> 00:26:43,825
It's a dwarf demon.

277
00:26:44,305 --> 00:26:45,705
Apasmarasur.

278
00:26:46,785 --> 00:26:51,265
A symbol of ignorance
and your memory loss.

279
00:26:53,065 --> 00:26:54,865
That which makes you
forget everything.

280
00:26:56,985 --> 00:26:59,665
Dignity, knowledge, education!

281
00:27:00,185 --> 00:27:02,225
Sometimes when the student...

282
00:27:02,905 --> 00:27:05,345
becomes a demon like Apasmarasur...

283
00:27:05,945 --> 00:27:07,825
then the teacher has to become
like Nataraj.

284
00:27:09,985 --> 00:27:12,825
You said I don't have the answers.

285
00:27:13,505 --> 00:27:17,345
I do have the answers.
I always did.

286
00:27:18,185 --> 00:27:21,385
But do you have the patience to
understand the answers?

287
00:27:21,865 --> 00:27:23,385
I have a lot of patience.

288
00:27:23,665 --> 00:27:26,785
But we have waited for this
for 75 years.

289
00:27:27,545 --> 00:27:29,185
Let's settle it today.

290
00:27:29,665 --> 00:27:30,665
What do you say?

291
00:27:31,065 --> 00:27:32,345
Okay.
Ask away.

292
00:27:32,665 --> 00:27:35,825
Right here.
In front of everyone.

293
00:27:36,265 --> 00:27:37,905
Great!
Alright.

294
00:27:43,465 --> 00:27:46,425
So, here's my question number one.

295
00:27:47,265 --> 00:27:51,065
The Sangh that Prof. Nadkarni
is such a huge fan of...

296
00:27:51,465 --> 00:27:53,145
Their claim to fame is...

297
00:27:53,785 --> 00:27:56,545
that they've been banned thrice.

298
00:27:56,945 --> 00:27:58,945
In fact, after Independence

299
00:27:59,385 --> 00:28:02,865
the Indian government
had immediately banned them.

300
00:28:03,145 --> 00:28:04,625
Am I right, sir?

301
00:28:04,945 --> 00:28:07,905
In 1948, after Gandhi's assassination.

302
00:28:11,145 --> 00:28:13,145
My question is very simple, sir.

303
00:28:13,745 --> 00:28:16,505
If the organisation that was banned
by the Indian government

304
00:28:16,625 --> 00:28:20,345
is not anti-national,
then what is it?

305
00:28:20,985 --> 00:28:21,705
Tell me, sir.

306
00:28:23,065 --> 00:28:26,505
You said the Indian government
had banned RSS.

307
00:28:27,865 --> 00:28:28,865
You are right.

308
00:28:29,985 --> 00:28:30,985
But...

309
00:28:32,065 --> 00:28:34,265
if the ban was justified...

310
00:28:34,385 --> 00:28:37,505
then why was it lifted?
What does it prove?

311
00:28:38,665 --> 00:28:39,865
Vicky.

312
00:28:40,585 --> 00:28:43,065
We didn't kill Gandhi.

313
00:28:45,425 --> 00:28:46,705
I have a question for you.

314
00:28:47,025 --> 00:28:52,505
Who was the first person
to mourn Gandhi's death?

315
00:28:53,545 --> 00:28:56,825
Guruji, there's a telegram
from the Delhi office.

316
00:28:57,145 --> 00:28:58,305
Gandhi is no more.

317
00:28:58,665 --> 00:28:59,745
Godse has...

318
00:29:00,945 --> 00:29:02,225
Ram!

319
00:29:03,785 --> 00:29:06,905
This is very unfortunate
for the nation.

320
00:29:10,425 --> 00:29:12,665
Halt all programmes.

321
00:29:13,625 --> 00:29:15,345
The country is in mourning.

322
00:29:16,145 --> 00:29:19,145
The Sangh will also be in mourning
for 13 days.

323
00:29:25,145 --> 00:29:27,945
"Om shanti om!"

324
00:29:28,145 --> 00:29:30,305
- "Om shanti om!"
- "Om shanti shanti!"

325
00:29:32,265 --> 00:29:34,065
(radio playing)

326
00:29:45,305 --> 00:29:47,984
Guruji, they're burning Brahmins
down in Pune.

327
00:29:47,985 --> 00:29:49,785
The fire will spread to Nagpur soon.

328
00:29:50,025 --> 00:29:51,664
We are concerned about your safety.

329
00:29:51,665 --> 00:29:52,984
We'll give them a fitting reply.

330
00:29:52,985 --> 00:29:54,585
(all agreeing)

331
00:29:57,065 --> 00:29:58,065
Quiet!

332
00:29:58,225 --> 00:29:59,225
Calm down.

333
00:29:59,745 --> 00:30:01,265
They are our people too.

334
00:30:02,865 --> 00:30:03,945
They've lost their way.

335
00:30:05,185 --> 00:30:08,065
We'll not respond to violence
with more violence.

336
00:30:08,585 --> 00:30:10,465
We too believe in non-violence.

337
00:30:13,145 --> 00:30:13,985
Guruji.

338
00:30:14,145 --> 00:30:15,305
Orders from higher authority.

339
00:30:15,545 --> 00:30:18,065
I have to arrest you.

340
00:30:18,345 --> 00:30:22,945
If my arrest brings peace
to the nation

341
00:30:23,505 --> 00:30:25,025
then I'm ready.

342
00:30:25,745 --> 00:30:27,145
Stop, Guruji!

343
00:30:28,145 --> 00:30:29,745
(indistinct chatter)

344
00:30:33,025 --> 00:30:35,345
Please break your vow of silence,
Mr. Golwalkar.

345
00:30:36,065 --> 00:30:38,705
Godse has admitted
that he was a member of the RSS.

346
00:30:39,345 --> 00:30:41,585
And the Sangh taught him
how to fire a gun.

347
00:30:42,985 --> 00:30:44,785
We just need a signature.

348
00:30:45,705 --> 00:30:47,785
Assume that you gave the orders.

349
00:30:48,745 --> 00:30:52,225
Godse had left the Sangh
many years back.

350
00:30:53,825 --> 00:30:56,705
He wants pure politics.

351
00:30:57,145 --> 00:30:59,545
And we want culture.

352
00:30:59,945 --> 00:31:02,545
The world will not understand
this technicality.

353
00:31:03,145 --> 00:31:06,505
The government believes
that crime festered in your backyard.

354
00:31:07,145 --> 00:31:09,145
If you don't take responsibility

355
00:31:09,385 --> 00:31:11,505
we'll destroy the Sangh completely.

356
00:31:11,785 --> 00:31:16,385
The Sangh is not a building
that you can destroy.

357
00:31:18,025 --> 00:31:19,745
It's a school of thought.

358
00:31:20,585 --> 00:31:21,905
It exists today.

359
00:31:22,945 --> 00:31:25,985
And it'll still exist in India
after 100 years.

360
00:31:29,145 --> 00:31:30,705
"Truth alone triumphs".

361
00:31:32,025 --> 00:31:36,305
Your Honour, I don't repent
anything I've done.

362
00:31:37,865 --> 00:31:39,065
One more thing.

363
00:31:39,745 --> 00:31:41,865
I had quit the Sangh
a long time back.

364
00:31:42,705 --> 00:31:44,945
Because I wanted to be active
in politics.

365
00:31:46,745 --> 00:31:48,305
That was my own decision.

366
00:31:49,305 --> 00:31:51,825
The act you are labelling
as crime...

367
00:31:52,625 --> 00:31:54,945
The honour of carrying it out
is mine alone.

368
00:31:55,545 --> 00:31:56,705
And I'm proud of it!

369
00:31:56,905 --> 00:31:59,064
Long live "Akandh Bharat",
undivided India!

370
00:31:59,065 --> 00:32:01,545
- Long live!
- Long live!

371
00:32:11,985 --> 00:32:13,304
So, according to you

372
00:32:13,305 --> 00:32:16,625
the RSS had nothing to do
with Gandhi's assassination.

373
00:32:16,945 --> 00:32:18,145
Please tell us the truth.

374
00:32:18,265 --> 00:32:20,985
Gandhi's spirit will sob
hearing your lies.

375
00:32:22,865 --> 00:32:25,065
Vicky, you're talking about Gandhi.

376
00:32:26,505 --> 00:32:31,945
Do you know what he thought
about the RSS?

377
00:32:36,625 --> 00:32:38,705
- Left, right, left.
- Left, right, left.

378
00:32:48,185 --> 00:32:50,345
RASHTRIYA SWAYAMSEVAK SANGH
BRANCH - WARDHA MAHARASHTRA

379
00:32:50,905 --> 00:32:54,425
You've been a part
of the Congress yourself.

380
00:32:55,265 --> 00:32:59,065
Then why didn't you establish
the Sangh with the Congress?

381
00:33:00,065 --> 00:33:01,865
If you'd done that

382
00:33:02,745 --> 00:33:06,025
the Congress could have
shared the blessings.

383
00:33:06,545 --> 00:33:08,065
I had tried.

384
00:33:08,665 --> 00:33:10,545
With Dr. Paranjape.

385
00:33:12,145 --> 00:33:13,225
But...

386
00:33:14,865 --> 00:33:16,785
We didn't succeed.

387
00:33:17,185 --> 00:33:19,025
Because of Laxmi,
the goddess of wealth?

388
00:33:19,505 --> 00:33:22,505
It was never about the money.

389
00:33:23,145 --> 00:33:25,065
It was a difference of principles.

390
00:33:25,985 --> 00:33:30,385
I believe the nation doesn't need
only politics.

391
00:33:31,145 --> 00:33:33,145
We need to build it
on character.

392
00:33:35,265 --> 00:33:40,065
Without any character, independence
would be reduced to an empty voice.

393
00:33:41,825 --> 00:33:43,705
It can still be heard.

394
00:33:45,545 --> 00:33:47,945
But it would lack strength.

395
00:33:50,665 --> 00:33:52,665
It is a very difficult path.

396
00:33:52,905 --> 00:33:55,625
The path of the truth
is always difficult.

397
00:33:57,145 --> 00:33:58,825
You already know that.

398
00:34:06,305 --> 00:34:08,225
July, 1949.

399
00:34:08,745 --> 00:34:10,425
The ban was lifted.

400
00:34:10,745 --> 00:34:13,665
Unconditionally...
Without any strings.

401
00:34:13,945 --> 00:34:16,065
You tell me, Vicky.
Why?

402
00:34:19,865 --> 00:34:20,865
Answer me.

403
00:34:21,505 --> 00:34:25,865
Because the Indian government
couldn't prove beyond doubt

404
00:34:26,185 --> 00:34:28,385
that the RSS is anti-nationalist.

405
00:34:28,545 --> 00:34:29,385
Right?

406
00:34:29,505 --> 00:34:31,425
Exactly.
Thank you.

407
00:34:33,425 --> 00:34:35,985
Now think calmly.

408
00:34:36,425 --> 00:34:38,345
If the ban was justified

409
00:34:38,785 --> 00:34:41,025
would the Indian government
lift the ban?

410
00:34:42,025 --> 00:34:43,825
Banning the RSS

411
00:34:44,905 --> 00:34:48,265
was considered ethically
and legally wrong.

412
00:34:48,625 --> 00:34:52,505
In spite of this,
the RSS has shown patriotism.

413
00:34:52,665 --> 00:34:55,185
Choosing non-violence over violence.

414
00:34:55,505 --> 00:34:56,665
Now you tell me.

415
00:34:57,065 --> 00:34:59,065
Is this behaviour anti-nationalist?

416
00:34:59,425 --> 00:35:02,065
Or is it the definition
of a true nationalist?

417
00:35:02,305 --> 00:35:03,305
Wow, sir!

418
00:35:04,065 --> 00:35:04,985
That's amazing!

419
00:35:05,385 --> 00:35:08,145
It'll be great fun to participate
in a debate with you.

420
00:35:08,265 --> 00:35:10,425
Can you calm down a bit, sir?

421
00:35:10,665 --> 00:35:12,784
Because when you get worked up

422
00:35:12,785 --> 00:35:15,185
you tend to slap people.

423
00:35:15,545 --> 00:35:16,824
What I mean to say is...

424
00:35:16,825 --> 00:35:18,545
Don't shoot the messenger.

425
00:35:18,865 --> 00:35:19,865
Okay, sir?

426
00:35:20,585 --> 00:35:23,385
Things like debate
are part of Western thinking.

427
00:35:24,065 --> 00:35:25,945
Debate means argument.

428
00:35:26,185 --> 00:35:32,025
India believes in "samvad"
that's constructive discussion.

429
00:35:33,025 --> 00:35:34,625
That's what we believe in.

430
00:35:35,505 --> 00:35:37,025
I have taught you this.

431
00:35:37,225 --> 00:35:43,185
Words and weapons roll off
an Indian's tongue with equal ease.

432
00:35:44,865 --> 00:35:48,065
Do you need more clarifications
to your first question?

433
00:35:48,425 --> 00:35:50,305
Or you can ask your next question.

434
00:35:55,505 --> 00:35:56,665
Okay. Okay.

435
00:35:57,025 --> 00:35:59,705
Let's give him the due advantage.

436
00:36:00,505 --> 00:36:04,944
The RSS had nothing to do with
Gandhi's assassination.

437
00:36:04,945 --> 00:36:05,985
But sir...

438
00:36:06,225 --> 00:36:08,185
What about 1975?

439
00:36:10,065 --> 00:36:11,065
Emergency.

440
00:36:11,185 --> 00:36:14,545
According to the order issued by
the Government of India

441
00:36:14,705 --> 00:36:17,385
all news mediums must

442
00:36:17,505 --> 00:36:23,065
seek approval before publishing.

443
00:36:24,865 --> 00:36:27,065
Who is Girish Nadkarni?

444
00:36:28,025 --> 00:36:28,864
It's me.

445
00:36:28,865 --> 00:36:31,585
Come with us.
We're here to arrest you.

446
00:36:31,705 --> 00:36:32,704
Father!

447
00:36:32,705 --> 00:36:34,345
(indistinct chatter)

448
00:36:35,345 --> 00:36:37,584
When the entire country
was burning...

449
00:36:37,585 --> 00:36:40,625
- Where are you taking him?
- Father!

450
00:36:41,185 --> 00:36:42,825
- Father!
- Let go!

451
00:36:47,825 --> 00:36:50,305
When the entire opposition
was in jail...

452
00:36:53,665 --> 00:36:57,225
Your leaders were writing letters
to Indira Gandhi.

453
00:36:58,025 --> 00:37:00,385
"Please... Let us go."

454
00:37:01,665 --> 00:37:03,545
"We'll not get involved in politics."

455
00:37:06,865 --> 00:37:09,425
Sir, this is my second question.

456
00:37:12,065 --> 00:37:13,585
Isn't it true?

457
00:37:14,225 --> 00:37:16,185
When it was time to fight

458
00:37:16,905 --> 00:37:19,025
the Sangh had taken the knee.

459
00:37:19,465 --> 00:37:20,905
What a shame!

460
00:37:22,465 --> 00:37:23,505
What a tragedy!

461
00:37:26,665 --> 00:37:28,945
You read the letters, Vicky.

462
00:37:30,385 --> 00:37:32,265
Not the thoughts behind them.

463
00:37:34,025 --> 00:37:36,265
You think it was fear?

464
00:37:38,385 --> 00:37:42,265
Thankfully during
Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj's time

465
00:37:44,185 --> 00:37:45,945
there was no social media.

466
00:37:47,025 --> 00:37:49,665
Otherwise these so-called Leftists...

467
00:37:50,745 --> 00:37:52,505
If they were present

468
00:37:53,625 --> 00:37:55,065
and got to know

469
00:37:55,305 --> 00:37:58,305
that Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj
is going to meet Afzal Khan

470
00:37:58,705 --> 00:38:00,065
they would've made hashtags.

471
00:38:00,225 --> 00:38:02,384
"Will Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj
bend the knee?"

472
00:38:02,385 --> 00:38:03,985
It would have gone viral.

473
00:38:06,785 --> 00:38:07,785
But Vicky...

474
00:38:08,385 --> 00:38:11,465
When a tiger pounces to kill
its enemy

475
00:38:11,745 --> 00:38:14,145
it first takes a step back.

476
00:38:14,425 --> 00:38:17,865
At that time, lakhs of swayamsevaks
were in jail.

477
00:38:18,065 --> 00:38:19,905
Their families were out
on the streets.

478
00:38:20,385 --> 00:38:21,385
Helpless.

479
00:38:22,065 --> 00:38:25,625
A general's duty
is not just to fight.

480
00:38:26,145 --> 00:38:29,705
It is also to protect his soldiers.

481
00:38:31,345 --> 00:38:32,345
Father.

482
00:38:32,585 --> 00:38:34,945
Everyone is saying you've done
something wrong.

483
00:38:35,385 --> 00:38:38,425
The police are saying you're an enemy
of the country.

484
00:38:39,265 --> 00:38:41,865
When the authorities are scared
of being questioned

485
00:38:42,185 --> 00:38:44,825
they turn the people who ask
the questions into enemies.

486
00:38:45,145 --> 00:38:46,425
Don't be scared.

487
00:38:46,825 --> 00:38:48,065
Never be afraid.

488
00:38:48,505 --> 00:38:51,825
You need the courage of a swayamsevak
to tell the truth.

489
00:38:52,305 --> 00:38:53,305
Remember that.

490
00:38:56,305 --> 00:38:58,025
Sulochana Nadkarni.

491
00:38:58,225 --> 00:38:59,465
GIRISH NADKARNI

492
00:39:02,425 --> 00:39:03,865
Mother, what's wrong?

493
00:39:07,545 --> 00:39:10,065
Your father is no more.

494
00:39:24,305 --> 00:39:25,825
That was strategy.

495
00:39:27,705 --> 00:39:30,945
To ensure thousands of fathers
could return home.

496
00:39:34,625 --> 00:39:36,905
So that those children
didn't become orphans.

497
00:39:38,785 --> 00:39:41,705
You call the RSS's action tragedy.

498
00:39:42,025 --> 00:39:44,465
Whereas it is the RSS
that saved this democracy.

499
00:39:45,185 --> 00:39:47,784
When I was in jail
during the Emergency

500
00:39:47,785 --> 00:39:50,785
I observed the swayamsevaks.

501
00:39:50,985 --> 00:39:52,785
When we were all put in jail.

502
00:39:53,065 --> 00:39:55,305
I saw how disciplined you were.

503
00:39:57,145 --> 00:40:02,025
Your sacrifice and your service
changed my mind.

504
00:40:02,305 --> 00:40:03,824
I noticed how,
even in captivity

505
00:40:03,825 --> 00:40:06,864
you set aside ideas of caste and creed
and remained united.

506
00:40:06,865 --> 00:40:10,745
I realised the future of the nation
is secure in your hands.

507
00:40:12,505 --> 00:40:16,344
Your contribution to the fight
against the Emergency

508
00:40:16,345 --> 00:40:19,065
would be etched in gold
on the pages of history.

509
00:40:19,225 --> 00:40:23,424
The maximum number of protestors
to be jailed were RSS workers.

510
00:40:23,425 --> 00:40:26,625
Without your cadres
and your organisation

511
00:40:26,945 --> 00:40:29,425
this revolution could never
be successful.

512
00:40:29,625 --> 00:40:32,864
You have sacrificed yourself
for the sake of democracy.

513
00:40:32,865 --> 00:40:35,625
The nation will
forever be in your debt.

514
00:40:41,545 --> 00:40:42,865
Emotional blackmail.

515
00:40:43,505 --> 00:40:45,185
These are all stories.

516
00:40:45,425 --> 00:40:46,985
He has no proof.

517
00:40:47,865 --> 00:40:51,465
Sir, if you're so honest
and if you have the guts

518
00:40:52,185 --> 00:40:54,385
then answer my third question.

519
00:40:56,185 --> 00:40:57,985
Year 1992.

520
00:40:58,185 --> 00:40:59,225
Babri Masjid.

521
00:41:00,225 --> 00:41:01,945
What was the strategy?

522
00:41:02,745 --> 00:41:04,745
That was a crime.

523
00:41:06,745 --> 00:41:08,905
Do you have the guts
to answer my question?

524
00:41:09,305 --> 00:41:10,545
What's going on?

525
00:41:13,025 --> 00:41:14,185
Sir, are you okay?

526
00:41:15,905 --> 00:41:17,904
What's going on?
Show's over.

527
00:41:17,905 --> 00:41:19,505
Everybody get back to class.
Come on.

528
00:41:29,345 --> 00:41:31,905
Ma'am does your wing
always interrupt?

529
00:41:32,545 --> 00:41:34,985
You'd lost
after asking your five questions.

530
00:41:36,185 --> 00:41:38,305
Remember, I saved you.

531
00:41:42,825 --> 00:41:43,825
Let's go.

532
00:41:53,705 --> 00:41:54,705
Ma'am.

533
00:41:55,145 --> 00:41:56,145
Vicky is losing it.

534
00:41:56,465 --> 00:41:58,025
He's digressing from the topic.

535
00:41:58,625 --> 00:42:00,025
Wrong place, wrong time.

536
00:42:00,745 --> 00:42:02,065
It was the right time.

537
00:42:02,705 --> 00:42:03,705
But the place was wrong.

538
00:42:04,345 --> 00:42:05,865
He is not lost, Ipshita.

539
00:42:06,985 --> 00:42:08,225
He is expanding.

540
00:42:09,905 --> 00:42:11,185
The boy has a lot of fire.

541
00:42:11,985 --> 00:42:14,905
And fire needs oxygen.

542
00:42:15,625 --> 00:42:16,625
What do you mean?

543
00:42:16,745 --> 00:42:21,625
This topic is too big
for the university campus.

544
00:42:22,545 --> 00:42:24,065
It needs to be on prime time.

545
00:42:30,865 --> 00:42:32,185
Hey babe, how are you?

546
00:42:33,225 --> 00:42:37,265
You know the coverage
of Mrs. Roy's books was incredible.

547
00:42:37,385 --> 00:42:38,184
Too good.

548
00:42:38,185 --> 00:42:39,265
Now, listen.

549
00:42:40,025 --> 00:42:43,185
I have gold for you.

550
00:42:50,745 --> 00:42:52,545
Our previous agendas
were not successful.

551
00:42:52,745 --> 00:42:54,625
That's why we couldn't topple
the government.

552
00:42:55,585 --> 00:42:57,225
There's a very important topic.

553
00:42:57,745 --> 00:43:00,344
We can expose the relationship
between the government and the RSS

554
00:43:00,345 --> 00:43:01,945
for political benefit.

555
00:43:02,265 --> 00:43:05,465
We can brew hatred in the hearts
of the citizens.

556
00:43:06,225 --> 00:43:08,425
We'll bring about change
with the power of the youth.

557
00:43:10,665 --> 00:43:13,185
Another thing...
We have a professor there.

558
00:43:13,945 --> 00:43:15,705
Pallavi Menon.

559
00:43:16,265 --> 00:43:17,945
Contact her and tell her

560
00:43:18,065 --> 00:43:20,585
to help all our people
in the college.

561
00:43:21,385 --> 00:43:22,905
The narrative should be set.

562
00:43:24,505 --> 00:43:27,945
This Prof. Nadkarni of the RSS...

563
00:43:28,065 --> 00:43:29,905
Assassinate his character.

564
00:43:31,905 --> 00:43:34,345
Give political support
to the student movement.

565
00:43:35,065 --> 00:43:37,745
Every person should be forced
to take sides.

566
00:43:38,145 --> 00:43:39,145
Our side.

567
00:43:44,025 --> 00:43:46,825
Mr. Aditya Rao.
I'm surprised.

568
00:43:47,065 --> 00:43:48,665
It took you so much time.

569
00:43:49,265 --> 00:43:51,065
I'm giving you a chance

570
00:43:51,705 --> 00:43:54,985
to be the face
of the biggest debate of the year.

571
00:43:55,345 --> 00:43:57,225
Student versus teacher.

572
00:43:57,945 --> 00:44:00,745
Left wing versus right wing.

573
00:44:00,865 --> 00:44:03,024
Student Vicky Hegde.

574
00:44:03,025 --> 00:44:05,664
- Teacher Prof. Dr. Gopal Nadkarni.
- Correct!

575
00:44:05,665 --> 00:44:06,505
My professor.

576
00:44:06,825 --> 00:44:10,985
Your ex-professor
who'll come to the debate--

577
00:44:12,065 --> 00:44:13,985
Firstly, this guy...

578
00:44:14,265 --> 00:44:15,984
The stunt that he has pulled...
he'll never come.

579
00:44:15,985 --> 00:44:17,065
Listen to me.

580
00:44:17,385 --> 00:44:19,585
Vicky Hegde has already
been convinced

581
00:44:19,705 --> 00:44:21,945
by my old classmate, Pallavi.

582
00:44:22,305 --> 00:44:24,025
He will come.

583
00:44:24,625 --> 00:44:26,065
And you bring Nadkarni.

584
00:44:26,305 --> 00:44:27,704
The debate is yours.

585
00:44:27,705 --> 00:44:31,704
Ms. Kavya Rawat, you've stopped him
from coming to this newsroom

586
00:44:31,705 --> 00:44:33,225
because he is from the RSS.

587
00:44:33,705 --> 00:44:36,025
And today you're inviting him
to this newsroom

588
00:44:36,425 --> 00:44:37,705
because he is from the RSS.

589
00:44:39,305 --> 00:44:40,305
How convenient!

590
00:44:42,505 --> 00:44:43,785
I'll talk to him.

591
00:44:44,825 --> 00:44:45,905
But don't play the ticker.

592
00:44:46,665 --> 00:44:48,785
Don't give me that look.
Been there and done that. Okay?

593
00:44:48,985 --> 00:44:51,545
I'll talk to him
and if it's a yes, okay.

594
00:44:52,745 --> 00:44:54,745
I'm telling you...
Okay?

595
00:44:56,545 --> 00:44:57,545
Play the ticker.

596
00:44:58,505 --> 00:44:59,505
It's a news channel.

597
00:44:59,945 --> 00:45:02,905
If there's no promotion,
there won't be any commotion.

598
00:45:03,345 --> 00:45:08,745
Bharat Express presents
the biggest debate of the year.

599
00:45:08,865 --> 00:45:10,185
Monday Battle Royale.

600
00:45:10,305 --> 00:45:12,465
This Monday at 12 noon.

601
00:45:12,665 --> 00:45:15,945
Can the teacher answer when the student
bombards him with questions?

602
00:45:16,145 --> 00:45:18,745
Don't forget to tune in.
Exclusively on Bharat Express.

603
00:45:18,865 --> 00:45:21,145
(students protesting)

604
00:45:28,145 --> 00:45:31,344
The administration of the Mumbai
Institute of Arts and Economics

605
00:45:31,345 --> 00:45:33,065
have been gheraoed.

606
00:45:33,305 --> 00:45:37,264
While the students protest violently,
the faculty also seem divided...

607
00:45:37,265 --> 00:45:39,345
...in their opinion.

608
00:45:40,865 --> 00:45:42,705
An absolute gridlock at CSMT.

609
00:45:42,825 --> 00:45:44,385
Protestors have occupied the tracks.

610
00:45:44,505 --> 00:45:47,825
Now the lifeline of the city
has come to a complete standstill.

611
00:45:48,145 --> 00:45:51,505
We have to be on high alert
in all these locations.

612
00:45:51,785 --> 00:45:54,144
Use force to stop, not to hurt.

613
00:45:54,145 --> 00:45:56,345
(students protesting)

614
00:46:02,505 --> 00:46:06,345
The area around the university has been
turned into a virtual fortress.

615
00:46:06,625 --> 00:46:10,025
Several clashes between the police
and the protestors have been reported.

616
00:46:10,305 --> 00:46:13,585
Police Commissioner has urged everyone
to maintain peace.

617
00:46:13,785 --> 00:46:17,065
But Vicky's supporters aren't ready
to back off.

618
00:46:17,305 --> 00:46:19,065
Would the police have to use force?

619
00:46:19,625 --> 00:46:21,345
The situation is rife with tension.

620
00:46:21,465 --> 00:46:24,265
(students protesting)

621
00:46:25,145 --> 00:46:26,505
Are you students or politicians?

622
00:46:26,665 --> 00:46:28,545
Why aren't you in college
and out here blocking traffic?

623
00:46:28,745 --> 00:46:31,425
Are you asking us
whether we are politicians or not?

624
00:46:31,545 --> 00:46:34,065
Can you ask Prof. Nadkarni
the same question?

625
00:46:34,465 --> 00:46:37,545
Then tell us
who is the real politician?

626
00:46:37,905 --> 00:46:41,505
Who is consciously injecting
the system with his own ideology?

627
00:46:41,625 --> 00:46:44,265
The citywide chaos
that you have created seems...

628
00:46:44,505 --> 00:46:46,145
...so performative and directionless.

629
00:46:46,345 --> 00:46:48,425
Our professor was the one
who created the scene.

630
00:46:48,705 --> 00:46:50,224
We have simply expanded our reach.

631
00:46:50,225 --> 00:46:51,904
So the entire nation has to listen.

632
00:46:51,905 --> 00:46:54,745
We're on the streets
because we have nothing to hide.

633
00:46:54,865 --> 00:46:58,624
Vicky is gaining support from
universities across the world.

634
00:46:58,625 --> 00:47:00,385
(students protesting)

635
00:47:20,625 --> 00:47:22,785
You've put on weight, sethji.

636
00:47:25,625 --> 00:47:27,345
Put the bag in the car's boot.

637
00:47:28,705 --> 00:47:31,265
Let your boss know
the job will be done.

638
00:47:42,665 --> 00:47:44,305
Look, Prof. Nadkarni.

639
00:47:45,265 --> 00:47:46,905
I have a lot of respect for you.

640
00:47:48,985 --> 00:47:51,985
But this is about
the university's reputation.

641
00:47:52,385 --> 00:47:55,305
I've been constantly getting calls
from the trustees.

642
00:47:55,745 --> 00:47:58,745
They want you to formally apologise.

643
00:47:59,345 --> 00:48:00,545
An apology letter.

644
00:48:01,665 --> 00:48:04,825
You can say you were angry and...

645
00:48:05,185 --> 00:48:07,785
And you took it out on the student
by mistake.

646
00:48:09,065 --> 00:48:10,065
Simple.

647
00:48:15,905 --> 00:48:18,945
You talk about respect
and then you take it away.

648
00:48:20,945 --> 00:48:22,145
Apology letter?

649
00:48:22,785 --> 00:48:26,025
What is the apology for?

650
00:48:26,625 --> 00:48:27,785
For telling the truth?

651
00:48:28,345 --> 00:48:31,305
Or for holding the mirror
to this ill-mannered student?

652
00:48:31,505 --> 00:48:34,545
Stop being so stubborn, Gopal.

653
00:48:34,665 --> 00:48:37,065
We're in the age of social media.

654
00:48:38,065 --> 00:48:40,785
Here the truth is not
what is actually true.

655
00:48:41,145 --> 00:48:44,185
Truth is what can be seen.

656
00:48:44,705 --> 00:48:46,705
That is how media's film works.

657
00:48:47,305 --> 00:48:48,705
And right now...

658
00:48:49,305 --> 00:48:53,305
You are looking like a villain
in this film.

659
00:48:58,625 --> 00:49:01,865
Maybe I'm the villain in your film.

660
00:49:03,945 --> 00:49:05,625
But did you know?

661
00:49:06,305 --> 00:49:12,465
I was the one
who suggested the apology letter.

662
00:49:13,905 --> 00:49:17,025
You'll be retiring in two years.

663
00:49:17,545 --> 00:49:21,025
We're talking
about your pension, Gopal.

664
00:49:21,145 --> 00:49:22,625
Think about it.

665
00:49:25,865 --> 00:49:27,185
Thank you for your concern.

666
00:49:29,065 --> 00:49:31,625
You're not the villain in my film.

667
00:49:36,745 --> 00:49:38,065
Then what am I?

668
00:49:39,465 --> 00:49:40,905
Please tell me.

669
00:49:43,345 --> 00:49:47,065
What do you think of me?

670
00:49:51,145 --> 00:49:53,785
I don't think about you at all.

671
00:49:56,665 --> 00:49:59,985
Mr. Nadkarni, we have to
protect our funding.

672
00:50:00,465 --> 00:50:02,145
Don't make me force my hand.

673
00:50:03,065 --> 00:50:04,265
Please sign the letter.

674
00:50:04,385 --> 00:50:05,385
Come on.

675
00:50:12,865 --> 00:50:15,625
This apology letter reminded me
of something else.

676
00:50:15,985 --> 00:50:20,224
Then you can become a "Maafiveer",
apologist-hero, like your own hero.

677
00:50:20,225 --> 00:50:23,065
The apology letter
you're talking about...

678
00:50:23,545 --> 00:50:26,025
Please do some research first.

679
00:50:26,545 --> 00:50:27,545
You'll understand.

680
00:50:29,065 --> 00:50:33,065
There's a reason why
a person is hailed a hero.

681
00:50:35,665 --> 00:50:37,945
As far as signing goes...

682
00:50:39,665 --> 00:50:40,945
Let me tell you a story.

683
00:50:41,345 --> 00:50:45,465
When it was time to pass the bar exam,
to become a lawyer...

684
00:50:45,865 --> 00:50:48,705
the British had given him a paper
in London...

685
00:50:49,065 --> 00:50:52,785
to write he'd never say
anything against the British.

686
00:50:53,345 --> 00:50:55,345
Only then would he be allowed
to pass the bar.

687
00:50:55,745 --> 00:50:56,985
They wanted him to sign it.

688
00:50:57,225 --> 00:50:58,225
Or else...

689
00:51:01,425 --> 00:51:05,265
Guess what your "maafiveer"
and my hero had said.

690
00:51:11,665 --> 00:51:12,665
This.

691
00:51:13,025 --> 00:51:14,185
That's what he did.

692
00:51:43,705 --> 00:51:44,785
I'll make some tea.

693
00:51:45,545 --> 00:51:46,545
Prabha.

694
00:51:46,745 --> 00:51:47,745
Please sit.

695
00:51:51,985 --> 00:51:53,865
Oh what fun!

696
00:51:55,145 --> 00:51:57,545
The professors in our university.

697
00:51:58,905 --> 00:52:00,585
They're very secular.

698
00:52:02,225 --> 00:52:05,585
But they were focussed
on violence today.

699
00:52:07,785 --> 00:52:10,625
So, instead of them,
I invoked Gandhi today.

700
00:52:12,065 --> 00:52:13,025
What?

701
00:52:13,385 --> 00:52:15,745
Non-cooperation movement.

702
00:52:16,225 --> 00:52:18,825
They asked me to give up
on my principles.

703
00:52:19,985 --> 00:52:20,985
So, I gave it to them.

704
00:52:22,185 --> 00:52:23,385
Resignation letter.

705
00:52:31,425 --> 00:52:34,265
Freshen up.
I'll get some tea for you.

706
00:52:37,985 --> 00:52:38,985
Prabha.

707
00:52:42,545 --> 00:52:45,985
I'll help you around the house
from tomorrow.

708
00:52:50,345 --> 00:52:54,025
Will he answer
all of his student's questions?

709
00:52:54,185 --> 00:52:58,625
Forget about answers,
the teacher has run off.

710
00:52:58,905 --> 00:53:01,024
He has tendered his resignation.
Why?

711
00:53:01,025 --> 00:53:04,985
If I were in Vicky's place,
I'd slapped Nadkarni back.

712
00:53:05,265 --> 00:53:08,224
We don't want his resignation.
We want a public apology.

713
00:53:08,225 --> 00:53:11,984
I want to ask
what has the RSS ever done.

714
00:53:11,985 --> 00:53:15,785
We can't find you anywhere
in the history books.

715
00:53:15,945 --> 00:53:18,425
Let me ask you a simple question.

716
00:53:18,745 --> 00:53:20,745
During the struggle
for independence...

717
00:53:20,865 --> 00:53:23,304
When the entire country
was in agony...

718
00:53:23,305 --> 00:53:25,144
When so many people were
sent to jail...

719
00:53:25,145 --> 00:53:28,024
There was bloodbath everywhere...

720
00:53:28,025 --> 00:53:29,944
Where was the RSS?

721
00:53:29,945 --> 00:53:31,625
Where were you hiding?

722
00:53:31,745 --> 00:53:33,424
In some room in Nagpur?

723
00:53:33,425 --> 00:53:34,864
We weren't hiding.
We were active.

724
00:53:34,865 --> 00:53:36,264
For you, struggle means

725
00:53:36,265 --> 00:53:39,225
either going to jail
or featuring in newspapers.

726
00:53:39,625 --> 00:53:41,464
There are different levels
of struggle.

727
00:53:41,465 --> 00:53:43,184
In the mind,
through speech and through actions.

728
00:53:43,185 --> 00:53:44,064
Are you aware?

729
00:53:44,065 --> 00:53:45,345
That's your way of thinking.

730
00:53:45,545 --> 00:53:47,904
You are confusing us with semantics.

731
00:53:47,905 --> 00:53:49,425
You are confused as it is.

732
00:53:49,705 --> 00:53:51,665
We're trying to explain things
to you.

733
00:53:52,465 --> 00:53:54,145
Dr. Keshav Hedgewar.

734
00:53:54,345 --> 00:53:57,065
He is respectfully referred to as
Doctor saab.

735
00:53:57,825 --> 00:53:59,785
Really sorry about this.

736
00:54:01,985 --> 00:54:05,265
My two P's, professionalism
and passion.

737
00:54:05,985 --> 00:54:07,225
I always get mixed up
in these.

738
00:54:08,905 --> 00:54:10,345
There's a third P.

739
00:54:11,025 --> 00:54:12,225
Psychosis.

740
00:54:13,625 --> 00:54:15,065
Don't mix that too.

741
00:54:18,065 --> 00:54:20,505
I am crazy.
Guilty as charged.

742
00:54:21,065 --> 00:54:23,625
But I can't help myself
when it comes to the truth.

743
00:54:24,065 --> 00:54:25,945
I have learnt it from you, sir.

744
00:54:26,465 --> 00:54:27,945
Always stand with the truth.

745
00:54:28,385 --> 00:54:31,065
I haven't always agreed with you.
And I won't.

746
00:54:31,505 --> 00:54:33,065
Sir, you're my professor too.

747
00:54:33,985 --> 00:54:35,185
You've been my teacher.

748
00:54:36,545 --> 00:54:39,905
Of course, I haven't agreed on
everything you've said and I won't.

749
00:54:42,465 --> 00:54:45,145
Please try to understand why
I'm doing this.

750
00:54:50,025 --> 00:54:51,025
Sir...

751
00:54:51,945 --> 00:54:54,185
Every time you spoke
about the country...

752
00:54:55,865 --> 00:54:57,425
Everything you said...

753
00:54:59,185 --> 00:55:00,065
It would touch us.

754
00:55:00,185 --> 00:55:01,785
I'd always thought...

755
00:55:02,345 --> 00:55:05,465
These thoughts should be shared
with the nation and the youth.

756
00:55:05,785 --> 00:55:06,785
Ma'am.

757
00:55:08,825 --> 00:55:09,865
I think this is...

758
00:55:11,425 --> 00:55:12,985
the right time for sir to...

759
00:55:37,265 --> 00:55:39,465
The national debate has been
scheduled for Monday.

760
00:55:39,865 --> 00:55:43,424
The Sangh doesn't have to justify
itself to anyone.

761
00:55:43,425 --> 00:55:44,465
Aditya.

762
00:55:44,785 --> 00:55:46,825
Right, sir.
I understand and I...

763
00:55:47,705 --> 00:55:49,224
But try to see it
from my perspective.

764
00:55:49,225 --> 00:55:51,185
It's his job to make empty noises.

765
00:55:52,265 --> 00:55:53,265
Not mine.

766
00:55:53,585 --> 00:55:55,505
He wants to create a scene, let him.

767
00:55:55,865 --> 00:55:57,984
I'm not part of his circus.

768
00:55:57,985 --> 00:55:59,385
But you are his teacher.

769
00:56:05,785 --> 00:56:07,425
He considers you his guru.

770
00:56:08,825 --> 00:56:11,505
And you treat him like a son.

771
00:56:15,065 --> 00:56:16,785
So, he's creating a scene.

772
00:56:17,345 --> 00:56:20,625
Who's responsible for
bringing him back to the class?

773
00:56:25,025 --> 00:56:26,945
(indistinct chatter)

774
00:56:53,705 --> 00:56:55,705
Hello, Mr. Vicky.

775
00:56:59,065 --> 00:57:00,065
Yes?

776
00:57:00,465 --> 00:57:01,545
I am Sohrab.

777
00:57:02,745 --> 00:57:04,545
Your well-wisher has sent me.

778
00:57:04,825 --> 00:57:06,985
I don't need any well-wisher.

779
00:57:10,985 --> 00:57:13,305
A lion hunts alone.

780
00:57:15,505 --> 00:57:17,705
But when there's a forest fire...

781
00:57:18,865 --> 00:57:21,025
even the lion burns.

782
00:57:22,025 --> 00:57:25,305
I'm only here to make sure

783
00:57:26,865 --> 00:57:28,745
the fire doesn't spread
to your home.

784
00:57:34,665 --> 00:57:36,025
This is my fight.

785
00:57:37,705 --> 00:57:39,625
And I'm not a sell-out.
Got it?

786
00:57:40,225 --> 00:57:41,665
That's what we want too.

787
00:57:42,505 --> 00:57:43,585
Don't sell out.

788
00:57:44,945 --> 00:57:46,265
Thank you for your visit.

789
00:57:58,185 --> 00:58:00,065
In our line of work

790
00:58:00,585 --> 00:58:02,345
very few people say thank you.

791
00:58:04,665 --> 00:58:07,425
Whether you fight
with or without our help...

792
00:58:08,025 --> 00:58:11,185
As long as the result is victory...

793
00:58:11,785 --> 00:58:12,785
I'm cool.

794
00:58:14,585 --> 00:58:15,945
Please remember one thing.

795
00:58:17,425 --> 00:58:20,184
My friends never lose.

796
00:58:20,185 --> 00:58:21,225
Got it?

797
00:58:48,065 --> 00:58:49,905
Why are you trying to be a hero?

798
00:58:55,345 --> 00:58:57,305
Can't you see what's going on?

799
00:59:01,225 --> 00:59:03,025
Vicky, this is not a debate.

800
00:59:03,385 --> 00:59:04,785
It's a riot.

801
00:59:07,025 --> 00:59:09,065
People have come to your home.

802
00:59:10,905 --> 00:59:11,905
Who was that man?

803
00:59:12,345 --> 00:59:13,625
What did he want?

804
00:59:15,505 --> 00:59:17,385
Saara, if I keep quiet too

805
00:59:17,945 --> 00:59:20,145
there'd be no difference between
them and me.

806
00:59:20,825 --> 00:59:23,145
Somebody has to cast
the first stone.

807
00:59:24,225 --> 00:59:25,585
But why you, Vicky?

808
00:59:26,185 --> 00:59:28,985
If not me, then who?

809
00:59:30,305 --> 00:59:31,465
Then who, Saara?

810
00:59:40,865 --> 00:59:46,024
The digital warriors on both sides
are prepared for the battle on Monday.

811
00:59:46,025 --> 00:59:48,944
This battle is not confined within
the college campus anymore.

812
00:59:48,945 --> 00:59:50,464
It has become
the spirit of the internet

813
00:59:50,465 --> 00:59:52,145
and a fight for identity.

814
00:59:52,345 --> 00:59:53,705
Is this a fair debate?

815
00:59:53,825 --> 00:59:57,545
Or has it turned into a televised
media trial of a young man's career?

816
00:59:57,665 --> 01:00:01,825
It's not just going to be a debate
but a live chargesheet.

817
01:00:02,065 --> 01:00:05,625
Will Nadkarni be able to face
these pointed questions?

818
01:00:07,745 --> 01:00:11,465
- Down with Nadkarni!
- Down with Nadkarni!

819
01:00:25,545 --> 01:00:27,065
They threw ink at you!

820
01:00:29,385 --> 01:00:32,185
Prabha, history as witness...

821
01:00:32,705 --> 01:00:36,025
whenever anyone tries
to soil the saffron

822
01:00:36,865 --> 01:00:39,425
history is written
with the same ink.

823
01:00:41,545 --> 01:00:44,065
Let there be 500 questions.

824
01:00:44,785 --> 01:00:49,065
I will answer
every last one of them.

825
01:00:58,265 --> 01:01:00,624
We're looking at
a student-teacher contract

826
01:01:00,625 --> 01:01:03,465
that has been shredded by
a single physical blow.

827
01:01:03,665 --> 01:01:07,145
Vicky Hegde has effectively turned
his research into a weapon

828
01:01:07,265 --> 01:01:09,905
against the very system
that has tried to silence him.

829
01:01:10,345 --> 01:01:12,825
He didn't just target
an organisation.

830
01:01:12,945 --> 01:01:14,425
He targeted a mindset...

831
01:01:15,025 --> 01:01:17,545
This boy isn't from Mumbai,

832
01:01:17,785 --> 01:01:19,065
I've seen him.

833
01:01:19,425 --> 01:01:21,265
Lay off the drugs.

834
01:01:21,385 --> 01:01:23,905
He is a student leader from Mumbai.

835
01:01:24,265 --> 01:01:25,425
Wait, let me show you.

836
01:01:25,825 --> 01:01:29,065
...will no longer be confined
to the classroom or the library.

837
01:01:29,385 --> 01:01:31,945
Bharat Express has announced
a special segment.

838
01:01:32,065 --> 01:01:33,945
Monday Battle Royale:
Guru versus student.

839
01:01:34,705 --> 01:01:37,305
A very important day.
A very important debate.

840
01:01:37,425 --> 01:01:39,984
With all eyes on Vicky
and Prof. Nadkarni.

841
01:01:39,985 --> 01:01:43,345
(students protesting)

842
01:01:53,665 --> 01:01:55,664
There's only one question
on everyone's mind.

843
01:01:55,665 --> 01:01:58,224
When will
this extraordinary debate start?

844
01:01:58,225 --> 01:02:01,424
Who will win this debate?
The student or the teacher?

845
01:02:01,425 --> 01:02:03,224
Questions will be asked with
an open mind.

846
01:02:03,225 --> 01:02:06,505
Will Prof. Nadkarni be able
to answer with the same openness?

847
01:02:06,745 --> 01:02:08,064
What will happen here today?

848
01:02:08,065 --> 01:02:11,345
Will Prof. Nadkarni be able
to answer Vicky's questions?

849
01:02:11,465 --> 01:02:15,465
Everyone is waiting eagerly for
Prof. Nadkarni and Vicky.

850
01:02:15,665 --> 01:02:18,465
There's heavy police posting here.

851
01:02:23,785 --> 01:02:26,065
(song playing)

852
01:03:19,465 --> 01:03:20,465
Where is he?

853
01:03:21,265 --> 01:03:22,264
Where is Nadkarni?

854
01:03:22,265 --> 01:03:23,864
Kavya, the professor
is not answering his phone.

855
01:03:23,865 --> 01:03:25,225
I think he's ghosting us.

856
01:03:25,625 --> 01:03:27,945
The show begins in 10 minutes.

857
01:03:28,345 --> 01:03:31,385
If he is not here by then
what will we telecast?

858
01:03:31,505 --> 01:03:32,385
An empty screen?

859
01:03:33,305 --> 01:03:35,305
The sponsors will chop my head off.

860
01:03:37,065 --> 01:03:39,025
Send a camera team to his house.

861
01:03:39,465 --> 01:03:41,785
Break the door if you have to.
Go!

862
01:03:42,545 --> 01:03:44,625
Go right now!

863
01:04:35,065 --> 01:04:37,985
The class will begin now
because the professor is here.

864
01:04:38,825 --> 01:04:39,825
Let's go.

865
01:04:46,265 --> 01:04:47,265
Everybody ready?

866
01:04:48,385 --> 01:04:50,225
We go live in...

867
01:04:51,425 --> 01:04:52,425
Three.

868
01:04:52,865 --> 01:04:53,865
Two.

869
01:04:54,465 --> 01:04:55,465
Go.

870
01:04:56,345 --> 01:04:57,345
And roll!

871
01:04:57,865 --> 01:04:59,825
Either the W's of journalism.

872
01:05:00,305 --> 01:05:02,185
Or the Night of Doom.

873
01:05:02,425 --> 01:05:04,184
Ministers in Parliament.

874
01:05:04,185 --> 01:05:06,664
Or the questions
of our favourite Vicky.

875
01:05:06,665 --> 01:05:08,304
They share one thing in common.

876
01:05:08,305 --> 01:05:10,504
That's five questions.

877
01:05:10,505 --> 01:05:12,705
And the five questions of
Judgement Day are...

878
01:05:12,985 --> 01:05:15,305
How did they live their life
on earth?

879
01:05:16,745 --> 01:05:18,705
How did they utilise their youth?

880
01:05:20,145 --> 01:05:22,225
How did they earn their wealth?

881
01:05:23,345 --> 01:05:25,345
How did they spend their wealth?

882
01:05:25,865 --> 01:05:28,465
And what did they do
with their knowledge?

883
01:05:34,345 --> 01:05:35,825
Just like this,
five questions...

884
01:05:36,185 --> 01:05:40,225
were asked by our govt.
to the opposition in May, 2024.

885
01:05:40,385 --> 01:05:41,385
First question.

886
01:05:41,985 --> 01:05:42,705
Triple Talaq.

887
01:05:44,345 --> 01:05:45,345
Second question.

888
01:05:45,665 --> 01:05:47,905
UCC: Uniform Civil Code.

889
01:05:48,185 --> 01:05:49,864
Third Question.
Surgical strikes.

890
01:05:49,865 --> 01:05:51,705
Fourth question.
Ram Mandir.

891
01:05:52,225 --> 01:05:53,145
Fifth question.

892
01:05:53,385 --> 01:05:55,265
Article 370.

893
01:05:56,145 --> 01:05:58,465
This is how
questions will be asked here today.

894
01:05:59,065 --> 01:06:01,664
Most importantly,
questions will be asked to

895
01:06:01,665 --> 01:06:05,185
Rashtriya Swayamsevak Sangh
that's RSS.

896
01:06:08,625 --> 01:06:11,145
We all know that the Sangh
has a few principles.

897
01:06:11,385 --> 01:06:14,384
One of which is not participating
in debates.

898
01:06:14,385 --> 01:06:15,905
And we totally respect that.

899
01:06:16,065 --> 01:06:18,144
But the situation
is a little different here.

900
01:06:18,145 --> 01:06:19,465
As things transpired...

901
01:06:19,665 --> 01:06:26,185
The questions were directed to
Vicky's thesis guide and mentor

902
01:06:26,385 --> 01:06:29,745
Dr. Prof. Gopal Nadkarni.

903
01:06:31,745 --> 01:06:35,465
There's something very interesting
happening here.

904
01:06:36,065 --> 01:06:40,785
If it were a five-day cricket match,
today would have been the third day.

905
01:06:41,065 --> 01:06:44,265
And it were a one-day match,
then I would have said...

906
01:06:44,465 --> 01:06:47,665
Welcome to the live telecast
of second innings.

907
01:06:48,065 --> 01:06:49,745
What happens
before the second innings?

908
01:06:51,265 --> 01:06:52,825
You know what happens.

909
01:06:53,225 --> 01:06:55,864
Here are the highlights
from the first innings.

910
01:06:55,865 --> 01:06:56,665
Have a look.

911
01:07:03,945 --> 01:07:06,344
So, here's my question number one.

912
01:07:06,345 --> 01:07:10,425
The Sangh that Prof. Nadkarni
is such a huge fan of...

913
01:07:10,825 --> 01:07:12,545
Their claim to fame is...

914
01:07:12,745 --> 01:07:15,225
that they've been banned thrice.

915
01:07:16,025 --> 01:07:18,985
In 1948,
after Gandhi's assassination.

916
01:07:19,745 --> 01:07:22,785
If the organisation that was banned
by the Indian government

917
01:07:24,145 --> 01:07:27,745
is not anti-national,
then what is it?

918
01:07:28,345 --> 01:07:30,905
We didn't assassinate Gandhi.

919
01:07:31,305 --> 01:07:33,345
July, 1949.

920
01:07:33,905 --> 01:07:35,825
The ban was lifted.

921
01:07:36,385 --> 01:07:39,305
Unconditionally...
Without any strings.

922
01:07:39,465 --> 01:07:40,984
Sir, this is my second question.

923
01:07:40,985 --> 01:07:42,705
What about 1975?

924
01:07:43,065 --> 01:07:43,985
Emergency?

925
01:07:44,345 --> 01:07:47,065
When the entire opposition
was in jail...

926
01:07:47,465 --> 01:07:50,945
Your leaders were writing
letters to Indira Gandhi.

927
01:07:51,065 --> 01:07:52,225
That was strategy.

928
01:07:52,665 --> 01:07:56,345
A general's duty
is not just to fight.

929
01:07:56,745 --> 01:08:00,265
It is also to protect his soldiers.

930
01:08:01,225 --> 01:08:02,545
BHARAT
EXPRESS

931
01:08:03,745 --> 01:08:05,185
Our constitution

932
01:08:05,905 --> 01:08:08,705
believes in free speech.

933
01:08:09,225 --> 01:08:12,345
If asking questions
is free speech

934
01:08:12,705 --> 01:08:14,665
then answering them
is also free speech.

935
01:08:19,705 --> 01:08:25,945
I'd like to tell the audience
that both Vicky and Prof. Nadkarni

936
01:08:26,065 --> 01:08:29,465
have refused to a judge's panel
or any kind of polling.

937
01:08:30,665 --> 01:08:33,145
I'd like to know why.

938
01:08:33,505 --> 01:08:36,505
I've asked him questions
for which he doesn't have an answer.

939
01:08:37,505 --> 01:08:38,665
That's the end of the story.

940
01:08:38,825 --> 01:08:43,625
Then how would you decide
whether you agree with his answers?

941
01:08:45,225 --> 01:08:46,945
Sir, do you want to take this?

942
01:08:52,385 --> 01:08:54,465
In "the Mahabharata", King Drupad...

943
01:08:55,185 --> 01:08:56,505
Drupad?

944
01:08:58,785 --> 01:08:59,785
Guys...

945
01:09:01,385 --> 01:09:02,665
That's Draupadi's dad.

946
01:09:07,265 --> 01:09:10,225
Drupad, Draupadi's father...

947
01:09:11,065 --> 01:09:12,945
wanted to slay Dronacharya.

948
01:09:13,225 --> 01:09:16,945
He raised his son, Dhrishtadyumna,
to defeat Drona.

949
01:09:17,185 --> 01:09:19,065
He was like our very own Vicky.

950
01:09:20,305 --> 01:09:23,905
He knew it would be no easy task.

951
01:09:24,705 --> 01:09:27,305
He went to Drona and said...

952
01:09:27,745 --> 01:09:29,425
"Please take me in as your disciple

953
01:09:30,025 --> 01:09:31,425
so that I can slay you."

954
01:09:33,065 --> 01:09:35,265
Dronacharya, even after
knowing this...

955
01:09:37,065 --> 01:09:38,465
... taught him everything.

956
01:09:38,905 --> 01:09:41,905
That's a teacher's responsibility.

957
01:09:42,665 --> 01:09:46,145
We trust our students.

958
01:09:46,545 --> 01:09:48,705
Even when they try to destroy us.

959
01:09:49,985 --> 01:09:51,545
Vicky has been my student.

960
01:09:52,065 --> 01:09:56,625
Although he's used my teachings
against me.

961
01:09:56,865 --> 01:09:59,425
But I still believe

962
01:10:00,505 --> 01:10:02,385
if I give him the correct answers

963
01:10:03,265 --> 01:10:05,625
he'll accept them in all honesty.

964
01:10:07,905 --> 01:10:09,785
It was not only your request.

965
01:10:10,705 --> 01:10:14,064
But the fact that there's still
some truth left in Vicky

966
01:10:14,065 --> 01:10:15,625
is what brought me here.

967
01:10:15,905 --> 01:10:16,665
Sir!

968
01:10:17,825 --> 01:10:25,065
When this "Dhrist-guy" fought Drona,
who won?

969
01:10:28,665 --> 01:10:30,345
You want to take that, Mr. Vicky?

970
01:10:33,145 --> 01:10:36,785
Drona dropped his weapon
believing in a lie

971
01:10:36,985 --> 01:10:39,385
and started meditating
on the battlefield.

972
01:10:39,825 --> 01:10:46,545
That's when Dhrishtadyumna
beheaded his teacher, Dronacharya.

973
01:10:50,865 --> 01:10:51,865
Aditya.

974
01:10:52,225 --> 01:10:53,265
Start with the questions...

975
01:10:53,665 --> 01:10:55,744
...before these two take out
their swords.

976
01:10:55,745 --> 01:10:57,264
Ask the questions.
Fast!

977
01:10:57,265 --> 01:10:59,505
In this epic battle
between truth and lies

978
01:10:59,625 --> 01:11:02,985
Vicky will now ask his third, fourth
and final question.

979
01:11:04,385 --> 01:11:05,385
Professor...

980
01:11:05,865 --> 01:11:10,185
Here's my third question
for your Sangh, your RSS.

981
01:11:33,625 --> 01:11:35,145
Babri Masjid!

982
01:11:37,425 --> 01:11:40,705
December, 1992.

983
01:11:41,985 --> 01:11:43,665
I want to ask all of you a question.

984
01:11:43,825 --> 01:11:48,905
Can anyone tell me
who demolished Babri?

985
01:12:06,625 --> 01:12:07,305
You?

986
01:12:12,505 --> 01:12:16,945
You've been an active volunteer
of the RSS.

987
01:12:19,145 --> 01:12:24,385
Was the destruction of the Babri Masjid
a pre-planned conspiracy?

988
01:12:26,665 --> 01:12:29,225
Please answer
and let's keep it simple.

989
01:12:30,745 --> 01:12:33,345
Just give us a yes or a no.

990
01:12:41,985 --> 01:12:43,025
Speak up, professor.

991
01:12:47,665 --> 01:12:51,385
If the RSS is a peaceful,
charitable organisation

992
01:12:51,545 --> 01:12:55,025
then why did its members
climb the dome?

993
01:13:03,145 --> 01:13:04,545
Why were the walls broken?

994
01:13:06,145 --> 01:13:07,305
Please tell us, professor.

995
01:13:10,265 --> 01:13:13,225
I'll ask you
the most important question.

996
01:13:13,385 --> 01:13:19,344
Do you, in any way, justify the actions
of the RSS committed on the day

997
01:13:19,345 --> 01:13:21,424
of the demolition of the Babri Masjid?

998
01:13:21,425 --> 01:13:23,385
Just say yes or no!

999
01:13:33,545 --> 01:13:38,025
I don't support any of the violent acts
of that day, Vicky.

1000
01:13:41,665 --> 01:13:42,665
Great!

1001
01:13:43,385 --> 01:13:44,385
Then say it.

1002
01:13:45,065 --> 01:13:48,065
Admit it that the RSS
committed a crime.

1003
01:13:49,025 --> 01:13:52,824
That the RSS demolished Babri Masjid
and the RSS is violent.

1004
01:13:52,825 --> 01:13:53,905
Just say it!

1005
01:13:54,385 --> 01:13:55,385
Just say it!

1006
01:14:03,545 --> 01:14:06,065
The RSS did not demolish any mosque.

1007
01:14:08,225 --> 01:14:11,265
There were protests
in front of Babri's structure.

1008
01:14:13,745 --> 01:14:16,225
But the structure didn't break...

1009
01:14:17,425 --> 01:14:19,664
when kar sevaks touched it.

1010
01:14:19,665 --> 01:14:21,305
It broke when

1011
01:14:21,905 --> 01:14:25,465
this nation's majority's trust
was broken.

1012
01:14:31,705 --> 01:14:34,145
Aditya, please pull up the slide.

1013
01:14:34,265 --> 01:14:35,265
Yes, sir.

1014
01:14:35,665 --> 01:14:36,905
Play the slide.

1015
01:14:47,705 --> 01:14:48,705
Take a look.

1016
01:14:52,785 --> 01:14:54,065
This section in the middle.

1017
01:15:03,625 --> 01:15:06,425
According to British records,
it's called 'Chhathi'.

1018
01:15:08,665 --> 01:15:10,065
Birthplace.

1019
01:15:11,865 --> 01:15:15,865
We didn't get permission to enter
our God's house.

1020
01:15:16,345 --> 01:15:18,065
What did our ancestors do?

1021
01:15:18,745 --> 01:15:22,745
They prayed outside
on this "Ram Chabutra".

1022
01:15:27,065 --> 01:15:29,465
Come rain or sunshine...

1023
01:15:30,145 --> 01:15:32,345
They waited for centuries.

1024
01:15:32,945 --> 01:15:36,745
Staring at that wall.

1025
01:15:38,025 --> 01:15:39,945
Hoping that one day
they'll be allowed inside.

1026
01:15:48,065 --> 01:15:50,945
They followed the law.

1027
01:15:53,385 --> 01:15:54,825
They waited patiently.

1028
01:15:55,625 --> 01:15:59,985
You're mourning the loss
of a 500-year-old building.

1029
01:16:01,505 --> 01:16:02,905
What about our faith...

1030
01:16:04,305 --> 01:16:08,145
That had been waiting forever
for its turn?

1031
01:16:09,705 --> 01:16:15,145
When the legal system fails
and days become years

1032
01:16:15,505 --> 01:16:18,385
then patience runs out.

1033
01:16:22,425 --> 01:16:24,745
And when patience runs out

1034
01:16:25,425 --> 01:16:28,865
then neither lives are spared
nor structures.

1035
01:16:29,025 --> 01:16:30,505
What structure?

1036
01:16:30,625 --> 01:16:32,225
Why aren't you calling
it the Babri Masjid?

1037
01:16:35,145 --> 01:16:36,305
Are you scared?

1038
01:16:36,465 --> 01:16:37,785
Are you ashamed?

1039
01:16:37,985 --> 01:16:41,345
Or was it your great RSS's holy war?

1040
01:16:49,185 --> 01:16:52,185
I am not calling it a mosque...

1041
01:16:53,425 --> 01:16:56,305
Because there are rules in Islam
about it.

1042
01:16:58,425 --> 01:17:03,145
And Babri does not follow them.

1043
01:17:04,905 --> 01:17:09,625
"Sahih al-Bukhari " and "Sahih Muslim"
both mention this.

1044
01:17:09,745 --> 01:17:13,145
Don't build mosques on graves.
It's forbidden.

1045
01:17:14,665 --> 01:17:16,345
According to "fiqh"

1046
01:17:16,505 --> 01:17:19,945
mosques are not to be built
on usurped land.

1047
01:17:20,145 --> 01:17:26,305
It states clearly
in Ibn Qudama's "Al-Mughni ".

1048
01:17:27,705 --> 01:17:28,945
Is that enough?

1049
01:17:29,545 --> 01:17:34,545
Or do you want me to give you
page numbers like Mr. Naik?

1050
01:17:40,745 --> 01:17:43,184
This is emotional manipulation.
Where are the facts?

1051
01:17:43,185 --> 01:17:44,145
He presented the facts.

1052
01:17:44,345 --> 01:17:45,824
He showed the map.
Talked about the history.

1053
01:17:45,825 --> 01:17:46,825
But the mosque was destroyed.

1054
01:17:47,025 --> 01:17:48,825
What about the belief
that was broken?

1055
01:17:49,185 --> 01:17:53,984
So, you're justifying
the RSS's actions, right?

1056
01:17:53,985 --> 01:17:59,305
If it is built on usurped land,
then the mosque is not valid, Vicky.

1057
01:17:59,625 --> 01:18:03,745
It was built on encroached land.

1058
01:18:04,185 --> 01:18:05,505
Taken land.

1059
01:18:05,905 --> 01:18:07,665
A land which others believe

1060
01:18:08,385 --> 01:18:10,265
is disputed land.

1061
01:18:11,665 --> 01:18:13,824
Even according to
Shariat law

1062
01:18:13,825 --> 01:18:17,145
such a building is never
considered a mosque.

1063
01:18:17,945 --> 01:18:20,745
It can only be called a structure.

1064
01:18:23,465 --> 01:18:25,905
India's Supreme Court...

1065
01:18:27,345 --> 01:18:30,305
The highest legal institution
of the country...

1066
01:18:31,865 --> 01:18:36,185
...has acknowledged that remnants
of a temple were found underneath.

1067
01:18:37,505 --> 01:18:39,945
The Archaeological Survey has shown

1068
01:18:40,145 --> 01:18:44,945
temple pillars, "kalash", "amalkas"

1069
01:18:45,225 --> 01:18:47,225
and shrine platform.

1070
01:18:47,665 --> 01:18:49,425
In 1976

1071
01:18:49,745 --> 01:18:54,225
KK Muhammad had proved
there was a temple under Babri.

1072
01:18:55,785 --> 01:18:58,305
How can I call it a mosque?

1073
01:18:59,425 --> 01:19:06,305
So, you're saying all this
to justify yourself, right?

1074
01:19:06,505 --> 01:19:09,305
I believe in the soil
of this country.

1075
01:19:11,065 --> 01:19:13,065
I believe in the wise sages...

1076
01:19:13,865 --> 01:19:15,905
Doesn't matter
whether they're Hindu or Muslim...

1077
01:19:16,265 --> 01:19:20,865
The ones who preach unity
and not politics.

1078
01:19:21,145 --> 01:19:24,545
This is my India.

1079
01:19:25,425 --> 01:19:32,625
And I'll always justify
the believers of this holy land.

1080
01:19:34,225 --> 01:19:37,265
You say the RSS demolished
a mosque.

1081
01:19:37,745 --> 01:19:39,065
I am saying...

1082
01:19:39,505 --> 01:19:42,665
India's faith was destroyed first.

1083
01:19:44,145 --> 01:19:48,865
The Sangh was just the last heartbeat
of centuries old ache.

1084
01:19:49,185 --> 01:19:55,385
In the last 100 years, the Sangh has
only been associated with one temple.

1085
01:19:55,985 --> 01:19:58,505
Ramjanmabhoomi,
birthplace of Ram.

1086
01:20:02,185 --> 01:20:04,865
And Vicky, there are two more sites.

1087
01:20:06,025 --> 01:20:08,545
Great if we get them cordially.

1088
01:20:09,025 --> 01:20:13,305
But if we have to fight,
we are ready.

1089
01:20:14,305 --> 01:20:17,945
This is a matter
of the nation's belief.

1090
01:20:19,225 --> 01:20:20,745
Did you get it, Vicky?

1091
01:20:21,865 --> 01:20:23,945
Say yes or no!

1092
01:20:41,905 --> 01:20:45,385
Friends, at this point
we'll take a break.

1093
01:20:45,505 --> 01:20:48,225
Please come back for more questions
on the other side.

1094
01:21:01,425 --> 01:21:02,465
BHARAT
EXPRESS

1095
01:21:04,305 --> 01:21:06,625
VICKY'S QUESTION ON RAM JANMABHOOMI
GETS FACTS FROM NADKARNI

1096
01:21:06,745 --> 01:21:08,624
What comes next in this debate?

1097
01:21:08,625 --> 01:21:10,704
The tension keeps rising
with every heartbeat.

1098
01:21:10,705 --> 01:21:13,025
I've never seen anything
quite like this before.

1099
01:21:13,305 --> 01:21:14,985
(students protesting)

1100
01:21:16,425 --> 01:21:17,784
The situation has taken a turn.

1101
01:21:17,785 --> 01:21:20,465
The prof's answers
has divided the crowd in two.

1102
01:21:20,745 --> 01:21:22,064
The crowd is growing.

1103
01:21:22,065 --> 01:21:24,064
The police barricade
is about to break.

1104
01:21:24,065 --> 01:21:27,665
We'll have to wait to see
how the police handle the situation.

1105
01:21:34,345 --> 01:21:38,185
Now, let's get to
your biggest defense.

1106
01:21:39,145 --> 01:21:40,465
Social work.

1107
01:21:44,265 --> 01:21:45,785
Ladies and gentlemen.

1108
01:21:46,465 --> 01:21:51,185
The Sangh proclaims to be the world's
largest voluntary organisation.

1109
01:21:51,545 --> 01:21:53,065
Selfless service.

1110
01:21:53,745 --> 01:21:55,625
Nation building.

1111
01:21:55,945 --> 01:21:59,425
Sounds great, doesn't it?

1112
01:22:01,625 --> 01:22:02,705
But professor...

1113
01:22:04,025 --> 01:22:06,945
There's a loophole in your greatness.

1114
01:22:08,345 --> 01:22:11,905
There's no documentation
of your great work.

1115
01:22:12,185 --> 01:22:13,705
Isn't that strange?

1116
01:22:17,945 --> 01:22:21,225
You claim to be running the country.

1117
01:22:28,265 --> 01:22:30,425
It is not a selfless service mission.

1118
01:22:31,265 --> 01:22:34,705
It's a convenient mask.
A facade.

1119
01:22:35,025 --> 01:22:40,225
For you and your Sangh
to hide behind.

1120
01:22:49,545 --> 01:22:53,145
This is known as social service.

1121
01:22:55,425 --> 01:22:56,905
Bravo!

1122
01:22:58,305 --> 01:23:00,905
Prof, may I come closer to you?

1123
01:23:01,305 --> 01:23:02,305
Please.

1124
01:23:03,745 --> 01:23:04,745
One second.

1125
01:23:14,345 --> 01:23:17,025
And this is the RSS's contribution.

1126
01:23:17,705 --> 01:23:18,745
Zero!

1127
01:23:22,065 --> 01:23:25,865
Are you fans of Aryabhatta?

1128
01:23:26,065 --> 01:23:29,505
Always stuck on zero.

1129
01:23:30,825 --> 01:23:31,825
That's all for now.

1130
01:23:33,785 --> 01:23:35,065
Brilliant!

1131
01:23:35,705 --> 01:23:38,825
That would leave a mark.

1132
01:23:39,505 --> 01:23:41,145
He's right.

1133
01:23:42,145 --> 01:23:44,545
Anyone can build castles in the air.

1134
01:23:45,025 --> 01:23:46,305
Where's the proof?

1135
01:23:47,265 --> 01:23:52,385
You're looking at social work
through corporate lenses.

1136
01:23:54,665 --> 01:23:56,425
There you need to show
proof of work.

1137
01:23:58,665 --> 01:24:00,305
We offer sacrifices.

1138
01:24:02,065 --> 01:24:05,145
We don't have
a centralised database.

1139
01:24:06,785 --> 01:24:09,825
Because we're swayamsevaks, volunteers.

1140
01:24:10,945 --> 01:24:12,545
Very convenient excuse, sir.

1141
01:24:14,025 --> 01:24:17,225
Burden of proof
is your responsibility.

1142
01:24:17,905 --> 01:24:20,545
Burden of accountability
belongs to the RSS.

1143
01:24:20,745 --> 01:24:23,625
What does responsibility mean?

1144
01:24:24,025 --> 01:24:27,385
Break the word down.

1145
01:24:28,505 --> 01:24:33,065
Responsibility is response
and ability.

1146
01:24:33,265 --> 01:24:34,945
The ability to respond.

1147
01:24:36,945 --> 01:24:38,625
In the hour of need

1148
01:24:38,785 --> 01:24:42,225
the first respondent is
not a guy in black suit.

1149
01:24:42,745 --> 01:24:45,305
Nor in white kurta.

1150
01:24:45,865 --> 01:24:48,064
They wear khaki pants.

1151
01:24:48,065 --> 01:24:50,985
You'd have known if you travelled
across the country.

1152
01:24:51,305 --> 01:24:53,865
Accountability?
For what?

1153
01:24:56,705 --> 01:24:57,785
For the cameras?

1154
01:24:58,865 --> 01:25:00,305
Tell me something, Vicky.

1155
01:25:00,945 --> 01:25:03,985
When someone is drowning
in a flood...

1156
01:25:05,345 --> 01:25:07,385
Or someone is dying of hunger...

1157
01:25:07,665 --> 01:25:11,545
Instead of helping him
should we take a selfie first?

1158
01:25:14,145 --> 01:25:16,785
Should we make a show
of his helplessness

1159
01:25:16,945 --> 01:25:21,065
so that it can trend
on social media?

1160
01:25:22,745 --> 01:25:27,905
This is your selfie culture
not the Sangh's.

1161
01:25:31,225 --> 01:25:32,225
Wow!

1162
01:25:32,785 --> 01:25:34,385
That's amazing, professor!

1163
01:25:34,865 --> 01:25:38,825
You should have been a politician
or an actor.

1164
01:25:39,265 --> 01:25:40,705
Why did you become a professor?

1165
01:25:41,225 --> 01:25:45,345
Thing is your big words
won't work anymore.

1166
01:25:46,985 --> 01:25:49,905
You did exactly what
the Sangh had done.

1167
01:25:51,145 --> 01:25:53,865
Lots of big words
but zero proof.

1168
01:25:57,065 --> 01:25:59,665
Fine.
You don't have proof.

1169
01:26:00,705 --> 01:26:04,945
But I have a video
that I would like to show you.

1170
01:26:06,985 --> 01:26:09,065
Could you please play
the tsunami video for us?

1171
01:26:11,345 --> 01:26:13,025
Play the video.

1172
01:26:31,905 --> 01:26:32,905
Stop!

1173
01:26:34,905 --> 01:26:38,505
After the natural disaster,
the local organisation is there.

1174
01:26:38,945 --> 01:26:40,785
They've reached there first.

1175
01:26:40,985 --> 01:26:42,785
And they're already helping
the locals.

1176
01:26:43,705 --> 01:26:48,185
You'd reached much later
with your flag. Right?

1177
01:26:50,145 --> 01:26:53,265
So many people lost their lives
that day.

1178
01:26:54,065 --> 01:26:56,385
Old people as well as children.

1179
01:26:58,345 --> 01:27:03,545
Only someone who's lost their child
would understand the pain.

1180
01:27:17,905 --> 01:27:20,064
- Yes?
- I'm Prashant. Nadkarni...

1181
01:27:20,065 --> 01:27:23,385
- Sorry, it's not that kind of show.
- Ma'am, please...

1182
01:27:23,505 --> 01:27:24,585
No callers allowed.

1183
01:27:25,025 --> 01:27:27,064
I'm sorry. No, no.
I'm sorry.

1184
01:27:27,065 --> 01:27:27,984
Patch the call.

1185
01:27:27,985 --> 01:27:30,984
Ma'am, it's very important.
Please let me speak to him.

1186
01:27:30,985 --> 01:27:32,265
- Ma'am, please.
- Okay.

1187
01:27:32,465 --> 01:27:33,465
Connecting.

1188
01:27:35,265 --> 01:27:36,265
Okay, Prashant.

1189
01:27:36,865 --> 01:27:38,505
You're live.
Please speak.

1190
01:27:38,705 --> 01:27:41,345
Hello, I'm Prashant.

1191
01:27:41,745 --> 01:27:43,745
I want to say something to Vicky.

1192
01:27:44,545 --> 01:27:48,385
Vicky, the person you're discussing
losing a child with

1193
01:27:48,865 --> 01:27:52,945
had himself lost his child
during the Mumbai floods.

1194
01:27:59,025 --> 01:28:01,465
(chanting funeral prayers)

1195
01:28:22,025 --> 01:28:24,025
He couldn't save his own child.

1196
01:28:24,145 --> 01:28:27,065
But he still saved another child.

1197
01:28:28,745 --> 01:28:33,225
Aditya, the other child was me.

1198
01:28:33,665 --> 01:28:36,585
That great man saved my life.

1199
01:28:41,305 --> 01:28:44,025
Mr. Nadkarni, please forgive me.

1200
01:28:44,345 --> 01:28:45,785
Accept my humble reverence.

1201
01:28:45,905 --> 01:28:47,185
Hey, you crazy boy.

1202
01:28:48,145 --> 01:28:49,625
Why are you apologising?

1203
01:28:51,825 --> 01:28:53,905
My Dhruv didn't die that day.

1204
01:28:56,065 --> 01:28:58,185
Only a father died that day.

1205
01:29:04,825 --> 01:29:08,865
A father had taken his last breath.

1206
01:29:09,905 --> 01:29:14,065
But the swayamsevak
was still breathing.

1207
01:29:16,625 --> 01:29:18,065
His name is Prashant.

1208
01:29:21,785 --> 01:29:25,065
Prashant, live a long life, son.

1209
01:29:27,825 --> 01:29:29,505
Be very successful.

1210
01:29:32,065 --> 01:29:33,745
Don't lose your way.

1211
01:29:46,585 --> 01:29:51,545
I'm not here to discuss my life
but to talk about the Sangh.

1212
01:29:54,265 --> 01:29:56,065
Please play the clip.

1213
01:29:56,385 --> 01:29:57,385
Okay.

1214
01:29:58,225 --> 01:30:01,425
Guys, play the video.

1215
01:30:46,985 --> 01:30:48,945
The footage you see...

1216
01:30:51,345 --> 01:30:55,625
These are examples of when
the camera was on by mistake.

1217
01:30:56,905 --> 01:31:00,865
Otherwise, there's no proof
of 99% of the work done.

1218
01:31:01,585 --> 01:31:06,025
When God is a witness
there's no need for proof.

1219
01:31:07,385 --> 01:31:09,784
I had taught you three things
about the Sangh.

1220
01:31:09,785 --> 01:31:10,905
Have you forgotten?

1221
01:31:11,065 --> 01:31:15,545
First, don't make a poster
out of helplessness.

1222
01:31:17,145 --> 01:31:18,185
Second.

1223
01:31:18,505 --> 01:31:20,905
Don't earn points
for acts of service.

1224
01:31:22,545 --> 01:31:24,505
Third and the most important point.

1225
01:31:25,505 --> 01:31:29,665
Only God is a witness
to acts of service.

1226
01:31:31,265 --> 01:31:35,225
There's no doubt
in the swayamsevak's heart.

1227
01:31:35,945 --> 01:31:37,585
Only resolve.

1228
01:31:40,505 --> 01:31:46,225
A swayamsevak chooses
a life of service for himself.

1229
01:31:48,265 --> 01:31:53,505
He doesn't act out of selfish needs.

1230
01:31:53,945 --> 01:31:58,025
But for selfless reasons for others.

1231
01:31:59,665 --> 01:32:01,625
You know all this, Vicky.

1232
01:32:01,945 --> 01:32:03,225
Even then?

1233
01:32:05,425 --> 01:32:09,905
Are you unable to see
or unwilling to see?

1234
01:32:22,065 --> 01:32:27,225
Vicky, hope you've got the answer
to your fourth question.

1235
01:32:27,585 --> 01:32:30,145
Or do you still have any doubt?

1236
01:32:31,625 --> 01:32:32,945
I hope you're satisfied.

1237
01:32:34,785 --> 01:32:38,745
And if you allow
can we take a break now?

1238
01:32:39,865 --> 01:32:41,065
There's no need to break.

1239
01:32:41,705 --> 01:32:42,945
Let's continue.

1240
01:32:47,425 --> 01:32:48,385
Audience.

1241
01:32:49,905 --> 01:32:51,665
It's time for the last question.

1242
01:33:24,825 --> 01:33:25,905
You must be feeling sad.

1243
01:33:27,985 --> 01:33:29,065
As you should.

1244
01:33:29,425 --> 01:33:31,425
Your opposition says...

1245
01:33:31,665 --> 01:33:37,585
Whenever their agenda fails,
they present a card in front of us.

1246
01:33:40,265 --> 01:33:42,265
Can anybody tell me
what that card is?

1247
01:33:48,145 --> 01:33:49,825
Which card am I talking about?

1248
01:33:51,465 --> 01:33:53,065
It's called the victim card.

1249
01:33:59,985 --> 01:34:01,785
They toy with us.

1250
01:34:03,305 --> 01:34:04,905
But kill their own.

1251
01:34:10,545 --> 01:34:13,065
And they do it

1252
01:34:13,185 --> 01:34:17,305
for our sympathy and so that
they can emotionally manipulate us.

1253
01:34:17,465 --> 01:34:18,865
Vicky!

1254
01:34:27,545 --> 01:34:31,825
Are you going to point a finger
at a swayamsevak's death?

1255
01:34:33,265 --> 01:34:34,345
Easy, professor.

1256
01:34:37,305 --> 01:34:41,024
Aditya, is this a boxing ring
or a media newsroom?

1257
01:34:41,025 --> 01:34:42,544
Please tell him.

1258
01:34:42,545 --> 01:34:44,185
Vicky, there's no need
to be sarcastic.

1259
01:34:44,345 --> 01:34:45,785
Stick to the debate, okay?

1260
01:34:46,265 --> 01:34:47,665
Present your point, please.

1261
01:34:51,625 --> 01:34:52,625
Take a look.

1262
01:34:55,025 --> 01:34:57,705
His name was Shrinath.

1263
01:34:59,305 --> 01:35:03,385
He was a dedicated swayamsevak.

1264
01:35:04,745 --> 01:35:07,145
But guess what happened to him.

1265
01:35:07,705 --> 01:35:09,585
He was hacked to death.

1266
01:35:16,825 --> 01:35:17,985
It's a tragedy.

1267
01:35:19,145 --> 01:35:21,825
But was it murder?

1268
01:35:21,985 --> 01:35:24,025
Or a political investment?

1269
01:35:26,945 --> 01:35:30,665
I believe he was killed.

1270
01:35:30,905 --> 01:35:31,905
Why?

1271
01:35:33,185 --> 01:35:37,585
So that these shameless people can
earn their votes over his dead body.

1272
01:35:39,825 --> 01:35:42,865
You manufacture a martyr
then you weaponise the grief.

1273
01:35:45,945 --> 01:35:48,185
And today, professor...

1274
01:35:49,985 --> 01:35:52,465
you must answer our questions.

1275
01:35:57,145 --> 01:36:01,385
I had five questions
but everything leads to this.

1276
01:36:01,545 --> 01:36:03,305
This very question.

1277
01:36:04,865 --> 01:36:08,065
This is final question.
This is my last question to you.

1278
01:36:12,825 --> 01:36:16,184
This isn't about Dronacharya
believing a lie.

1279
01:36:16,185 --> 01:36:17,985
Nor is it about
a teacher and his student.

1280
01:36:18,225 --> 01:36:20,704
This is about every Indian citizen.

1281
01:36:20,705 --> 01:36:22,065
Every one living in India...

1282
01:36:22,185 --> 01:36:23,985
...whom they have lied to.

1283
01:36:24,625 --> 01:36:27,505
And today you must answer
for this, professor.

1284
01:36:27,705 --> 01:36:28,985
At any cost.

1285
01:36:48,825 --> 01:36:51,305
You called our sacrifice
a business, Vicky.

1286
01:36:53,305 --> 01:36:54,505
I'll remember that.

1287
01:37:01,025 --> 01:37:02,025
Play this.

1288
01:37:09,745 --> 01:37:11,505
Aditya, are you crazy?

1289
01:37:12,185 --> 01:37:15,065
We can't play something
that hasn't been vetted.

1290
01:37:15,465 --> 01:37:16,905
We don't know what's on it.

1291
01:37:17,185 --> 01:37:18,785
It could be hate speech.

1292
01:37:19,065 --> 01:37:20,785
It could be graphic violence.

1293
01:37:21,305 --> 01:37:24,025
We cannot do this, Aditya!

1294
01:37:29,905 --> 01:37:32,185
Will you trust your teacher
this time?

1295
01:37:32,705 --> 01:37:33,705
Always, sir.

1296
01:37:34,665 --> 01:37:35,665
Play it.

1297
01:37:46,985 --> 01:37:48,665
(crowd protesting)

1298
01:37:49,265 --> 01:37:50,545
Madam, are you from the media?

1299
01:37:51,785 --> 01:37:53,265
That is not Vicky Hegde.

1300
01:37:54,065 --> 01:37:55,545
He is lying, madam.

1301
01:37:55,945 --> 01:37:57,145
Vicky Hegde.

1302
01:37:57,825 --> 01:37:59,145
It’s a lie, madam.

1303
01:37:59,745 --> 01:38:01,145
Just hold on, ma'am.

1304
01:38:01,825 --> 01:38:02,865
What are you saying?

1305
01:38:03,385 --> 01:38:05,305
He is not Vicky Hegde!

1306
01:38:05,825 --> 01:38:07,265
Ma'am, I'll call you back.

1307
01:38:08,585 --> 01:38:10,385
Come with me.
Let’s go!

1308
01:38:10,745 --> 01:38:11,745
Okay.

1309
01:38:20,425 --> 01:38:25,825
Today this man,
in front of the whole world...

1310
01:38:27,265 --> 01:38:30,145
has maligned the character
of the RSS.

1311
01:38:32,905 --> 01:38:38,385
Now the country will judge
on the basis of evidence.

1312
01:38:39,825 --> 01:38:41,305
Not on theories.

1313
01:38:42,025 --> 01:38:43,025
Vicky.

1314
01:38:43,505 --> 01:38:46,545
This is the final answer
to your final question.

1315
01:38:47,145 --> 01:38:48,745
This is it.

1316
01:39:38,745 --> 01:39:42,145
(chanting religious slogans)

1317
01:39:58,825 --> 01:39:59,825
Pause.

1318
01:40:03,265 --> 01:40:04,665
Vicky, did you hear that?

1319
01:40:06,425 --> 01:40:07,865
Did you all hear that?

1320
01:40:09,945 --> 01:40:11,305
Did you hear what they said?

1321
01:40:13,585 --> 01:40:16,145
Did you hear
what those murderers said?

1322
01:40:16,745 --> 01:40:18,305
Do you at least agree on that?

1323
01:40:20,505 --> 01:40:22,185
Yes or no?

1324
01:40:30,865 --> 01:40:34,065
You don't have to belong
to the Sangh.

1325
01:40:36,265 --> 01:40:39,705
If you're an Indian citizen...

1326
01:40:40,225 --> 01:40:42,305
If you're a true patriot...

1327
01:40:43,065 --> 01:40:44,465
Then answer me this.

1328
01:40:45,065 --> 01:40:47,505
Does this sound
like the Sangh's slogan?

1329
01:41:03,065 --> 01:41:04,545
The Palakkad Case judgement.

1330
01:41:06,345 --> 01:41:08,384
Six out of the seven accused
were sentenced to death.

1331
01:41:08,385 --> 01:41:09,745
One was a minor.

1332
01:41:10,065 --> 01:41:11,785
Read the court records.

1333
01:41:14,145 --> 01:41:16,905
The killers were not
our people, Vicky.

1334
01:41:19,145 --> 01:41:20,985
They were political extremists.

1335
01:41:22,865 --> 01:41:24,985
You wanted a pattern.

1336
01:41:27,465 --> 01:41:29,065
Here's your pattern.

1337
01:41:31,225 --> 01:41:33,185
November 15, 2021.

1338
01:41:35,465 --> 01:41:37,065
Mambaram, Palakkad.

1339
01:41:37,945 --> 01:41:39,065
Sanjith.

1340
01:41:41,025 --> 01:41:42,945
He was travelling with his wife.

1341
01:41:46,865 --> 01:41:48,425
They stopped his motorbike.

1342
01:41:48,625 --> 01:41:51,145
And hacked the husband
in front of the wife.

1343
01:41:52,985 --> 01:41:55,905
Was that stage-managed martyrdom?

1344
01:41:58,345 --> 01:42:00,145
March, 2002.

1345
01:42:00,385 --> 01:42:01,385
Melur.

1346
01:42:02,505 --> 01:42:04,665
CK Sujeesh and P Sunil.

1347
01:42:05,585 --> 01:42:06,665
Double murder!

1348
01:42:07,985 --> 01:42:09,065
Midnight attack.

1349
01:42:12,465 --> 01:42:17,145
The RSS didn't pass judgement on this.
The Supreme Court did.

1350
01:42:25,225 --> 01:42:27,745
January 6, 2025.

1351
01:42:29,505 --> 01:42:30,985
Conditions upheld.

1352
01:42:38,265 --> 01:42:39,825
Have you heard of Dadu Singh?

1353
01:42:43,145 --> 01:42:44,745
Konde, Chhattisgarh.

1354
01:42:45,665 --> 01:42:48,065
Maoists killed him.

1355
01:42:48,385 --> 01:42:49,265
Why?

1356
01:42:50,985 --> 01:42:55,785
Because he was talking about
the country in LWE area.

1357
01:43:00,465 --> 01:43:02,585
You can check all this
on the internet.

1358
01:43:08,945 --> 01:43:10,465
Look at T Ashwini Kumar.

1359
01:43:15,425 --> 01:43:17,545
Look at R Rudresh in Bengaluru.

1360
01:43:36,465 --> 01:43:40,025
Vicky, I didn't expect this
from you.

1361
01:43:43,425 --> 01:43:45,305
I've taught you about all this.

1362
01:43:48,065 --> 01:43:49,905
Did you forget everything
so quickly?

1363
01:43:52,065 --> 01:43:54,425
We didn't kill Shrinath.

1364
01:43:57,545 --> 01:43:59,065
We lost him.

1365
01:44:12,065 --> 01:44:13,785
Please understand this.

1366
01:44:17,905 --> 01:44:20,385
The Sangh doesn't do anything
just because they want to.

1367
01:44:27,505 --> 01:44:29,265
The Sangh only does...

1368
01:44:32,505 --> 01:44:34,785
whatever is necessary
for the country.

1369
01:44:38,265 --> 01:44:41,705
It's been like this
for the last 100 years.

1370
01:44:43,665 --> 01:44:46,385
That's why the Sangh exists.

1371
01:44:49,545 --> 01:44:53,025
The day there is a swayamsevak
in every house...

1372
01:44:53,465 --> 01:44:56,905
we won't need the Sangh anymore.

1373
01:45:00,265 --> 01:45:02,265
When people have differences...

1374
01:45:03,265 --> 01:45:05,305
terror runs through their mind.

1375
01:45:06,425 --> 01:45:08,465
When people come together...

1376
01:45:10,905 --> 01:45:12,505
It's called the Sangh.

1377
01:45:18,985 --> 01:45:21,745
These two words oppose each other.

1378
01:45:25,145 --> 01:45:27,465
And you're trying to connect them.

1379
01:45:33,825 --> 01:45:35,585
Vicky, this is not
the Sangh's answer.

1380
01:45:35,945 --> 01:45:38,225
It is India's.

1381
01:45:39,145 --> 01:45:40,705
Of every Indian.

1382
01:45:43,185 --> 01:45:45,225
Now, the decision is yours, son.

1383
01:45:47,985 --> 01:45:50,225
(song playing)

1384
01:46:03,025 --> 01:46:04,185
Vicky.

1385
01:46:05,665 --> 01:46:07,945
(song continues)

1386
01:47:02,465 --> 01:47:05,185
- (all) Hail Mother India!
- Hail Mother India!

1387
01:47:32,505 --> 01:47:36,785
You don't look as happy
as you should be.

1388
01:47:39,065 --> 01:47:40,265
He knew.

1389
01:47:41,225 --> 01:47:44,985
He knew I had everything
on the Shrinath murder case.

1390
01:47:48,425 --> 01:47:50,065
I was the one who told him
about it.

1391
01:47:51,745 --> 01:47:53,025
Then...

1392
01:47:53,825 --> 01:47:56,345
How could it be his final question?

1393
01:48:09,585 --> 01:48:10,585
Who is he?

1394
01:48:11,025 --> 01:48:12,225
He is from Palakkad.

1395
01:48:12,345 --> 01:48:15,265
And what he's saying will
burn our entire theory to ashes.

1396
01:48:16,065 --> 01:48:17,064
Speak.

1397
01:48:17,065 --> 01:48:21,265
Madam, the boy who is on TV
is not Vicky Hegde.

1398
01:48:21,585 --> 01:48:24,385
I've known him since childhood.

1399
01:48:24,705 --> 01:48:26,825
He is Shrinath’s son.

1400
01:48:28,505 --> 01:48:30,665
- Shrinath?
- Yes, ma'am.

1401
01:48:30,785 --> 01:48:31,785
RSS worker?

1402
01:48:31,905 --> 01:48:32,905
Yes.

1403
01:48:33,305 --> 01:48:34,665
The one who was murdered?

1404
01:48:36,825 --> 01:48:37,825
Oh my God!

1405
01:48:40,185 --> 01:48:42,065
He played...
He played us all.

1406
01:48:59,985 --> 01:49:03,425
The environment
is a valuable resource.

1407
01:49:03,545 --> 01:49:07,025
(all) The environment
is a valuable resource.

1408
01:49:07,705 --> 01:49:10,145
Trees are a source of life
and oxygen.

1409
01:49:10,265 --> 01:49:13,425
(all) Trees are a source of life
and oxygen.

1410
01:49:13,665 --> 01:49:14,905
Class dismissed, ma'am?

1411
01:49:15,185 --> 01:49:16,185
Yes.

1412
01:49:17,505 --> 01:49:18,145
Let's go.

1413
01:49:19,785 --> 01:49:22,065
(song playing)

1414
01:50:53,345 --> 01:50:54,065
Vicky.

1415
01:50:56,985 --> 01:50:58,705
Mission RSS is complete.

1416
01:50:59,145 --> 01:51:00,464
What next?

1417
01:51:00,465 --> 01:51:02,065
Project "Ashtalakshmi".

1418
01:51:02,265 --> 01:51:04,665
That's the Seven Sisters.

